{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do","id":105041,"title":"What Should Lunars Be Able to Do? What Should They Not Be Able to Do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-03T13:20:08-07:00","id":105041,"title":"What Should Lunars Be Able to Do? What Should They Not Be Able to Do?","content":"This is the thread where we talk about what Lunars should (and should not) be able to do. The focus is <i>what we want to see 3rd Edition</i> and I hope to see many <i>example powers and abilities</i>. I'd also like to see the powers remain in the E1 - E5 range.<br /> <br /> Try not to just say that you want to see Lunars use elemental abilities as everyone will imagine that differently, but talk about how those powers will manifest.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> I'd like it if my Lunar could transform into a black wolf made of smoke. This would make them harder to see at night, let them squeeze under the cracks of a door to break into a place, and make sure they leave no footprints or other signs of physical disturbance. I don't imagine that they could choke/smother someone with their smoke self or that it would be any tougher/faster than a regular wolf form.<br /> <br /> I think Lunars should have powers that protect from the Wyld. I'd like to be able to bless a house or building so Wyld-tainted creatures either struggled to cross the threshold or experienced constant pain/damage while within. Mirroring Luna's ability to call the Wyld to her, I'd like a social based power that draws Fae (or other Wyld born things) to me. I imagine a sort of Lunar pied piper whose music is so haunting that Fae feel compelled to seek them out, only for the Lunar to slay them.<br /> <br /> I'd like more powers that allow me to influence and command terrestrial spirits. For example, I could call upon a raven spirit to spy for me or bring a message to my friend. Or tell the spirit of a forest that it should attempt to confuse and mislead anyone entering it for the next day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:41:47-07:00","id":105058,"title":"","content":"I want ... well basically the powers from Changeling: the Lost. Lunars should be allowed to be trickster, coming both from their adaption to the Wyld and their patron. They should be - for example - be capable of basic Talecrafting (in the Bordermarches, as their own lower powered WST). <br /> Then I'd really like to have more Charms allowing you to mix your other shapes or even combine them, so you end up stronger then any single form you collected so far. Take a claw from that form, the size from that form and the wings from the third one. I know this is possible already, but I do think this could really benefit from more (and earlier) Charms. One of these Charms should allow you to permanently upgrade or change your true form.<br /> <br /> I'd also really like to have Lunars a &quot;big gun&quot; similar to SMA, Solar Circle Sorcery, Shinmaic Charms (if they still exist), whatever Infernals will have and so on. Not really as a power for the players but to give a young Lunar something to strife for. Lunars have Knacks (if that's still a thing) and their shapeshifting, but those aren't endgame Charms. Sure, higher Essence gives any of your powers a boost as a Lunar, and high essence Charms are effective... but most of them are not reality-shattering cool.<br /> <br /> Oh and on a more abstract level: Lunars should not be able to get upgrades (as in forms) without paying exp. That just cheapens their shapeshifting alltogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:51:18-07:00","id":105067,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>About elementals, can I say I hope we <i>at least</i> get the basic effects of Hearth-and-Flame Shell, even if we don't get Essential Mirror Form to go with it? Meaning, you can take the form of a fire elemental, and if you do, you acquire its elemental nature and are made of fire, and anyone trying to grapple with you will be severely burned - but aside from the transformation itself, you don't gain any special powers or Charms that fire elementals have?</li> <li>And I hope we remain free to apply the flame transformation to any other form, using something like HBR, so that those with eagle spirit shapes can now be flame-eagles, smoke eagle, jade eagle, etc.?</li> <li>Lastly, it'd be nice to be able to assume behemoth-sized forms at a slightly lower Essence, it being thematic in the &quot;mythical god-beast&quot; way they're going for.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:56:34-07:00","id":105070,"title":"","content":"Can I put a spin on it? Because I wanted to create the very same thread, but you've beat me to it.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to know, what people think Lunars should do, that is not a some form of shapechanging. Because at this point what we do know, is that shapeshifting is one of their abilities, but not the end-all and the source of their abilties, just one of their tools. So in a doomed attempt to find the Lunar &quot;core&quot;, the mysterious Lunar theme that informs us about all of their abilities, maybe it's good to forget about shapeshifting for a second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-03-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:13:51-07:00","id":105077,"title":"","content":"Some non-shapeshifting things Lunars should be able to do:<br /> <br /> <b>- Watchful Spider Stance</b>: When activated, a Lunar can track down anything within her territory as though it were in her immediate location.<br /> <b>- Sense Borrowing Method</b>: The Lunar touches a target and then can experience everything they do as long as the motes remain committed.<br /> <b>- God Cutting Essence</b>: Allows the Lunar's attacks to inflict aggravated damage on spirits.<br /> <b>- Perfect Symmetry</b>: Turns the Lunar into a total hottie.<br /> <b>- Creating the Wolf, Feeding the Bear</b>: Causes groups of people to either experience intense fear or intense craving, ether generally or for a specific target.<br /> <br /> Yes, shapeshifting is an awesome general ability, but no one is talking about getting rid of Lunar charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:31:32-07:00","id":105095,"title":"","content":"May be have power over the forms of other beings, such as hiding their army of barbarian warriors as ravens or shooting beams of moonlight that force mutation in an opponent. But where as fair folk want to sow random chaos, Lunars are focused on particular change that they can control the fight with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:12:11-07:00","id":105115,"title":"","content":"Weather control.<br /> Seriously, I want Lunars being able to call storms and lightning. Their themes include being the force of nature. Also because it's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:17:42-07:00","id":105121,"title":"","content":"I'd like it if that Charm to scar people, and create obvious emotional connotations for the scars, made it through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:26:34-07:00","id":105133,"title":"","content":"I'm recently reading some stuff with Blood and Smoke Gangrel and Nosferatu, and I'm kind of feeling like I want stuff that goes with that.<br /> <br /> Claws to rend skin and leave blackened veins, resilience sufficient not just to ward off damage but to run right through it (I'd see Solars more as bouncing back against the force of attacks or being able to keep going if run through, and Lunars as more like the boar that just runs along your weapon to gore you), being able to rapidly reshape themselves to get through every obstacle and impediment while chasing you down, flashing a smile of glinting teeth that fills you with dread, going still and quiet and unseen in the manner of eyes in the dark, so,ething that creeps right up close to lick you or stroke you....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:31:39-07:00","id":105135,"title":"","content":"I think there might also be some elements salvageable from the Protean Keyword... not so much for animals, but for other shapes, something that emphasizes the sense that you can take that form because you overcame what had it originally in some manner... that certain stolen shapes provide certain bonuses to resonant Lunar Charms used while in them.<br /> <br /> It would play into that thing John once said about the Othermoons, how it was supposed to be that consuming them emphasized and enhanced some quality of Luna's rather than giving her new powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:35:02-07:00","id":105136,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand Ex3 will reshape the Lunars based on the mythical beast archetype (if such thing exists). I love this! So lunars are more similar to the minotaur, the hydra, enkidu, garuda, etc than to silver haired hercules. Maybe that was the intention since 1st ed, but I feel like a lot of &quot;werewolftheapocalypsisms&quot; distorted the idea. I think lunars are no changing breeds, I believe that they need to be able to build their own beastial form and they better get a lot of options that go beyond turning into athropomorphic animals. Lunars should be known by mortals as giant snakes with unbreakable silver scales that protects a ruin, mysterious shamans always surrounded by birds, a black dog armored in shadows that protects a village, the thief whose coming is always announced by mice and rats escaping the city. Maybe their charms could help them create this mythos around them and become guardians, scourges or simply legends all over creation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:41:05-07:00","id":105138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105136#post105136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand Ex3 will reshape the Lunars based on the mythical beast archetype (if such thing exists). I love this! So lunars are more similar to the minotaur, the hydra, enkidu, garuda, etc than to silver haired hercules. Maybe that was the intention since 1st ed, but I feel like a lot of &quot;werewolftheapocalypsisms&quot; distorted the idea. I think lunars are no changing breeds, I believe that they need to be able to build their own beastial form and they better get a lot of options that go beyond turning into athropomorphic animals. Lunars should be known by mortals as giant snakes with unbreakable silver scales that protects a ruin, mysterious shamans always surrounded by birds, a black dog armored in shadows that protects a village, the thief whose coming is always announced by mice and rats escaping the city. Maybe their charms could help them create this mythos around them and become guardians, scourges or simply legends all over creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider this before you try to tar and feather W:TA.<br /> <br /> Mythological Gaia is known for throwing monsters at problems. This is pretty much entirely her method of dealing with the problem of universal imbalance in Werewolf, too - make some monsters and get them on it. So this is where we get an intersection with mythological monsters and the Exalted that were based on Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:48:22-07:00","id":105141,"title":"","content":"flow and stretch like water, travelling along the ground or spiralling through the air thrusting out a limb that moves like it has a mind of its own while you come in from another angle<br /> <br /> descend like a flock of ravens, your weapon as the tip of every beak, your movement as the fluttering of innumerable wings that can't be followed<br /> <br /> blows thrust deep into the body, possibly leaving venemous barbs behind<br /> <br /> your enemy thinks they have you in hand, only for you to cast off your skin and dance backwards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:59:07-07:00","id":105146,"title":"","content":"* The return of Inevitable Spoor Discovery, but with writing that makes it clear that the Charm not only allows the Lunar to detect smells which no longer exist (or which effectively never existed), but also filters out all other conflicting scents (past and present) to focus solely on those of creatures. The Charm already does these things, but the flavor text and mechanical text do little to highlight how the Charm is more advantageous than merely using a dog's nose.<br /> <br /> * A <i>visual </i>version of Inevitable Spoor Discovery that detects tracks, even those that no longer exist. Footprints, handprints, fingerprints, faceprints (because sometimes, you get up close and personal with the ground), and tire tracks -- all of these become so apparent to the Lunar's eyes that they might as well glow. While far more limited in discerning the identity of those who interacted with a scene than Inevitable Spoor Discover, &quot;Ghost-Track Kenning&quot; would be infinitely more useful for reconstructing the events that took place at the scene. Which could be represented as a dice-result enhancer for the relevant Investigation action.<br /> <br /> * Likewise, perhaps a visual version of Blood On The Wind, which makes the Lunar an unshakable tracker once she discovers a visual trail. (Naturally, &quot;Ghost-Tracking Ken&quot; would allow her this start even when no such trace exists, just as ISD would enable Blood On The Wind even without an existing initial scent.)<br /> <br /> * A Perception Charm of indefinite duration which alerts the Lunar whenever anyone is observing her. This is like Observed Prey Instinct from First Edition, but without a dice-roll. It automatically reacts to any level of scrutiny, going quiet immediately if someone only glances at you for an instant and remaining pricked if someone continues to watch you. It doesn't tell you who, how, where or why someone is watching you or eavesdropping on you, but it DOES tell you exactly how many people are doing so.<br /> <br /> * A Manipulation Charm that revolves around preternatural body language, convincing any who see the Lunar that she is beneath their notice. Whether she is a rat or a servant or a literal elephant in the room, they dismiss her as unimportant. (Just because Lunar magic is all about Being Seen does not mean that Lunars can't be misleading about what they appear to be.)<br /> <br /> * Naturally also the opposite, a Charisma Charm like Solar Authority-Radiance Stance which the Lunar uses to convince people she's The Boss Of Them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-03-2014, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:05:25-07:00","id":105154,"title":"","content":"I believe Lunars should be able to threaten Solars in single combat. Bear in mind, I still acknowledge Solars as the undisputed masters of Abilities--A Melee-focused Solar should have the upper hand in a sword duel with a Lunar--but &quot;fighting in general&quot; is not an Ability. If Solars are mythical heroes, and Lunars are mythical monsters, then it must be acknowledged that, sometimes, the monsters are more than a match for the heroes. Odysseus, for all his cleverness, could not overcome Scylla and Charybdis: He could only minimize the damage they did. Beowulf, for all his strength, needed Wiglaf's help to slay the dragon, and he still lost his own life in the process. The gods of Asgard, for all their power, are fated to die at Ragnarok, devoured by wolves and serpents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:16:37-07:00","id":105159,"title":"","content":"I want them to be able to turn the weapons and skills of the enemy against them, by becoming them and more.<br /> <br /> In turn I want to be able to mix my shapes as I see fit, and have what I can turn into have tangible and awesome effects/powers.<br /> <br /> If I turn into a Tyrant Lizard/Furnace Rhino combo wreathed in spectral flame, I want to be able to mix and match powers from each of those to create this awesome form, not just aesthetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:27:09-07:00","id":105167,"title":"","content":"Throw a punch or swing a sword with such strength that a shockwave of raw force strikes a distant enemy.<br /> <br /> Turn into a heady, dark cloud like the Nue.<br /> <br /> Breathe nightmares into the minds of sleepers.<br /> <br /> Fill an attack with hidden power, shattering teeth with a kiss and denting armour with pebbles.<br /> <br /> Weather and absorb incoming attacks, charging up a monstrous counter.<br /> <br /> Raise a zombie from a corpse using parasitic wasp larvae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T17:23:54-07:00","id":105208,"title":"","content":"I'd like that if my Lunar runs into or is ambushed by a monster or Exalt, fights them in an epic duel, defeats them, rips open their chest, raises their bloody heart up in prayer to Luna, and then consumes it, I get to gain their shape. As opposed to only being able to do it if I spend 12-(a roll) hours spying on them first. After all, Lunars are supposed to be about adaptability.<br /> I understand that the writers don't want you to just go into a pet shop, vacuum everything up into your mouth and get their shapes, but surely there's another way to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T18:47:50-07:00","id":105298,"title":"","content":"The ability to design a 'mythic' beast as a spirit shape(s). In 2e if your spirit shape is say a lion you're only ever going to be using that to turn into a regular lion, a huge lion (Ox Expansion), or a were-lion, none of which except maybe the huge lion really feel that mythic, and only the were-lion is actually effective and it feels more D&amp;D-fantasy than ancient myth, and you're never going to get the ability to turn into the nemean lion with its impenetrable hide (I mean you can use soak charms but you can do that in any form). I've said it before but turning into a god-bull and trampling your enemies like king Narmer (<a href=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e7/Narmer_Palette_serpopard_side.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedi...opard_side.jpg</a>) feels a lot more mythic shapeshifter than turning into a half-man/half-bull for stat-buffs and stabbing them with an oversized sword. Making this work would also require having a tyrant lizard-based spirit-shape not automatically be better than a lion/bull/wolf-based spirit-shape for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-03-2014, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T19:25:49-07:00","id":105310,"title":"","content":"The ability to disrupt social scene by making it's all about them:<br /> <br /> &quot;So nice weather tod........I totally ship Chompy and Twilight Baker&quot;<br /> &quot;Nuh-uh, Twilight Baker already has a lover, the local Dragon-Blood dictator !&quot;<br /> &quot;You know what, our friendship is OVAAR!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T19:31:13-07:00","id":105313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105310#post105310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability to disrupt social scene by making it's all about them:<br /> <br /> &quot;So nice weather tod........I totally ship Chompy and Twilight Baker&quot;<br /> &quot;Nuh-uh, Twilight Baker already has a lover, the local Dragon-Blood dictator !&quot;<br /> &quot;You know what, our friendship is OVAAR!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Every thread eventually becomes a Lunars thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T20:29:12-07:00","id":105337,"title":"","content":"I doubt many would agree, but I'd prefer if they didn't have any powers resembling outright mind control. Instead, maybe they should just be highly resistant to such powers. Lunar influence should be about raw charisma and animal magnetism. Controlling other people like puppets seems more in line with the themes of the darker, more sinister Exalt types, and Sidereals... but I repeat myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-03-2014, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T20:45:17-07:00","id":105347,"title":"","content":"I think that's something they're reducing in the setting anyway, to avoid all the &quot;mind-rape&quot; issues. Same with Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T21:37:08-07:00","id":105364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105133#post105133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm recently reading some stuff with Blood and Smoke Gangrel and Nosferatu, and I'm kind of feeling like I want stuff that goes with that.<br /> <br /> Claws to rend skin and leave blackened veins, resilience sufficient not just to ward off damage but to run right through it (I'd see Solars more as bouncing back against the force of attacks or being able to keep going if run through, and Lunars as more like the boar that just runs along your weapon to gore you), being able to rapidly reshape themselves to get through every obstacle and impediment while chasing you down, flashing a smile of glinting teeth that fills you with dread, going still and quiet and unseen in the manner of eyes in the dark, something that creeps right up close to lick you or stroke you....</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105141#post105141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">flow and stretch like water, travelling along the ground or spiralling through the air thrusting out a limb that moves like it has a mind of its own while you come in from another angle<br /> <br /> descend like a flock of ravens, your weapon as the tip of every beak, your movement as the fluttering of innumerable wings that can't be followed<br /> <br /> blows thrust deep into the body, possibly leaving venemous barbs behind<br /> <br /> your enemy thinks they have you in hand, only for you to cast off your skin and dance backwards</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually kinda reminds me of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XiMJCspS9Fc\" target=\"_blank\">Alucard</a> from Hellsing, my immediate reaction would be to call him an Abyssal, but reading your list of cool abilities I would say that he passes pretty well as a Lunar. I also love Raven and Wolf from the comic &quot;East of West&quot;. The idea of a shaman who is just as comfortable as a flock of ravens or pack of wolves as they are in a individual form is really interesting to me! <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://thetelltalemind.files.wordpress.com/2013/09/east.jpg?w=487\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T02:15:01-07:00","id":105453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105364#post105364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This actually kinda reminds me of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XiMJCspS9Fc\" target=\"_blank\">Alucard</a> from Hellsing, my immediate reaction would be to call him an Abyssal, but reading your list of cool abilities I would say that he passes pretty well as a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'm seeing him more as Infernal.<br /> <br /> Picturing the Captain as a Lunar informs a couple of them, but not much of what I'm saying here.<br /> <br /> Notably, when I say stuff like &quot;descend like a flock of ravens&quot;, I don't mean literally transforming into a swarm of animals; I mean it as you kind of come in as a blurring motion, where you strangely <i>look</i> like a flock of ravens, down to the outlines of your blurry self seeming to resemble beaks and talons and wings, and conveying qualities of attack and defense that might emerge from that, while still being in the shape of a person.<br /> <br /> Likewise that idea of fluidly spiraling through the air: I remember a time I saw a documentary about some particularly vicious squid, that kept attacking the documentary shooters, and I'm drawing on the image of what a human shape moving and attacking like that would be (water or no water).<br /> <br /> Animal tropes in names and effects of Charms is hardly exclusive to Lunars, and was never really done well in Second Edition, but I think it has some potential if one goes with some really literal interpretations of metaphors, while still having the Lunar in human shape while doing them. I imagine it as both distinct, and uncanny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T03:36:35-07:00","id":105471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105453#post105453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, when I say stuff like &quot;descend like a flock of ravens&quot;, I don't mean literally transforming into a swarm of animals; I mean it as you kind of come in as a blurring motion, where you strangely <i>look</i> like a flock of ravens, down to the outlines of your blurry self seeming to resemble beaks and talons and wings, and conveying qualities of attack and defense that might emerge from that, while still being in the shape of a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of a lunar turning into an actual swarm of ravens to torment a city or to turn into a swarm of rats to spread a disease. The Lunars are going to be the mythological monster in 3e, and I like that, but creatures like the Stymphalian Birds, The Harpies hnd the Frog Plague from the old testament have their numbers as a part of their iconography (no one in Greek Mythology meets a single Stymphalian Bird after all), I think it should at least be possible to play as a swarm of... something for a lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:02:29-07:00","id":105480,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying that they couldn't <i>also</i> turn into a literal swarm of animals, mind.<br /> <br /> Just trying to think of suitable motifs for Charms that evoke transformation or bestiality without just being shapeshifting, since Lunars still need actual Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:51:15-07:00","id":105504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105154#post105154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Lunars should be able to threaten Solars in single combat. Bear in mind, I still acknowledge Solars as the undisputed masters of Abilities--A Melee-focused Solar should have the upper hand in a sword duel with a Lunar--but &quot;fighting in general&quot; is not an Ability. If Solars are mythical heroes, and Lunars are mythical monsters, then it must be acknowledged that, sometimes, the monsters are more than a match for the heroes. Odysseus, for all his cleverness, could not overcome Scylla and Charybdis: He could only minimize the damage they did. Beowulf, for all his strength, needed Wiglaf's help to slay the dragon, and he still lost his own life in the process. The gods of Asgard, for all their power, are fated to die at Ragnarok, devoured by wolves and serpents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the basic statement here (Lunars should give Solars a good solid fight in a straight matchup) though I'm a little wary of the examples being brought up. I've seen some folks around my local area and on some other forums try to use them to justify houserules putting Lunars where Solars USED to be in the tiering list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T05:07:07-07:00","id":105508,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the swarm of animals thing seems very Lunar to me. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I kind of like drawing on the tales of shifting gods of various mythologies for Lunar inspiration, so that its not just about changing and animals but it isn't just coming out of left field either. One of the things I've noticed in those tales is that the figures often just do something and the story doesn't even try to give details. So they do things like open locks by touching them, make pieces of the world out of small objects, walk through walls or just appear, etc. We never really hear how, because obviously they are gods and we are not meant to know their ways, it is enough to know that they did this. Tellingly, their shapeshifting isn't treated as anything separate from this, its just another secret they know.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to fit it back into transformational themes, you could say they know the secrets to transforming the world too (there's very little that couldn't be stated in those terms), but however you spin it I like the feel of that simple mystery. The Solars excel, the Sidereals exploit, the Lunars do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T05:13:36-07:00","id":105513,"title":"","content":"Swarms of things=rad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T05:40:47-07:00","id":105519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105513#post105513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarms of things=rad</div> </div> </div> </div>The Writer has spoken, Half Life 3 Confirmed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T05:43:50-07:00","id":105521,"title":"","content":"Should Lunar have Healing Charms ?<br /> <br /> What does Lunar's Crafting Charms look like ?<br /> <br /> Wait, those questions look oddly familiar....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:03:45-07:00","id":105529,"title":"","content":"As the unkillable monster archetype, Lunars should definitely have self-healing charms at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:15:43-07:00","id":105535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105529#post105529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the unkillable monster archetype, Lunars should definitely have self-healing charms at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have real Medicine charms this time then I hope it's some kind of Love-Coloured Healing Shower Light instead of Flesh Sculpting Art :'P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:23:18-07:00","id":105541,"title":"","content":"I'm still stuck on &quot;Lunars should be able to be Alex Mercer.&quot; Not in the bizarre inhuman parts but in the way that his &quot;war form&quot; is a human and he just adds mutations like giant shovel claws and stuff as he needs them. &quot;Urban predator&quot; is not a term that should be reserved solely for Changing Moons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:27:48-07:00","id":105546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105535#post105535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they have real Medicine charms this time then I hope it's some kind of Love-Coloured Healing Shower Light instead of Flesh Sculpting Art :'P</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Flesh-Sculpting Art, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T08:25:41-07:00","id":105584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105480#post105480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that they couldn't <i>also</i> turn into a literal swarm of animals, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105471#post105471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of a lunar turning into an actual swarm of ravens to torment a city or to turn into a swarm of rats to spread a disease. The Lunars are going to be the mythological monster in 3e, and I like that, but creatures like the Stymphalian Birds, The Harpies hnd the Frog Plague from the old testament have their numbers as a part of their iconography (no one in Greek Mythology meets a single Stymphalian Bird after all), I think it should at least be possible to play as a swarm of... something for a lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know they can do that already in 2E, right? There are a couple of knacks for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T08:33:42-07:00","id":105587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105584#post105584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know they can do that already in 2E, right? There are a couple of knacks for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not, actually.<br /> I got into Exalted about two weeks after 3e was announced, so I only own two books (why buy new books if a new edition is coming)<br /> Still, with their theme being changed a bit (or maybe it's just getting a strict theme and sticking with it), I'd like it if they kept this knack, because it's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 04-04-2014, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:41:56-07:00","id":105650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105521#post105521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Lunar have Healing Charms ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lick Wound from 1e, except good?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does Lunar's Crafting Charms look like ?<br /> <br /> Wait, those questions look oddly familiar.... </div> </div> </div>Tool-Hand Technique from 1e, except etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:14:25-07:00","id":105666,"title":"","content":"I could see some healing Charms that branch off from Halting the Scarlet Flow, allowing a Lunar to feed someone their blood like it was a burning hot panacea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:17:54-07:00","id":105670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105650#post105650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lick Wound from 1e, except good?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know that First Edition Lunar is not exactly what you call well-make, but do they actually have a charm name like that....... ? @_@<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:30:18-07:00","id":105677,"title":"","content":"Yes, they did, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:32:24-07:00","id":105679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105670#post105670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that First Edition Lunar is not exactly what you call well-make, but do they actually have a charm name like that....... ? @_@</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a second tier Charm with the awesome capability to... maybe prevent infections in others. The imagery of breathing opalescent mist onto a wound was nice, but as you can see, 1e had the most mechanically underwhelming Charms of all. Mutations were often more effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:50:47-07:00","id":105702,"title":"","content":"I brought this up in the other Lunars thread, though it got buried under a fresh wave of lapidary minutiae.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the core conceptual issue that their theme cannot be applied reasonably to all areas of character competence. By this I mean, Solars have the theme of &quot;superhuman excellence&quot;. All of their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply superhuman excellence to task X?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have the theme of &quot;manipulating destinies both of events and of things&quot;. All of their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply manipulating destinies to task X?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Abyssals have the theme of &quot;power over death and the dead&quot;. All of their Charms are built by sticking the Mirror keyword onto Solar ones. But going forward, their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply power over death and the dead to task X?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Infernals have the theme of &quot;exotic powers derived from the creators of the universe&quot;. All of their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply exotic powers derived from the creators of the universe to task X?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded have the theme of &quot;control over the elements, both the physical ones and their spiritual abstractions&quot;. All of their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply control of physical or spiritual abstractions of the elements to task X?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the theme of &quot;shapeshifting into animals and creatures of legend&quot;. Shapeshifting is an extremely broad tool, to be certain, but it also completely lacks ways to apply itself to things like crafting and lore, while in other areas like medicine its applications are limited to maybe one thing. It's also absurdly frontloaded, with pretty much everything you could do with shapeshifting given to you either at chargen or within a very small number of Charms and Knacks to unlock types of forms. Lunars end up having to make up for the missing areas of competence, and the need to have more than five Charms in their entire Exaltation, by being Silver Solars.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting is not a theme, it's a tool, and one that cannot carry the weight of an entire Exaltation on its back. Lunars need to have a theme in which shapeshifting is a thematically appropriate tool sometimes, rather than making it the crux of their existence. As it stands, though, I'm not sure I can even say Lunars should exist as Exalted at all, if their theme can't support everything an Exalt needs to be capable of doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:03:34-07:00","id":105721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105702#post105702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidereals have the theme of &quot;manipulating destinies both of events and of things&quot;. All of their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply manipulating destinies to task X?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that's loose at best.<br /> <br /> I mean, Sidereals &quot;manipulate destiny&quot; to perform <i>specific</i> tasks to generate specific destinies. Or they perform actions that are kind of weirdly tied alongside resonant destinies tangentially. Or they just plain tie certain things up in certain narrative roles, or even just use oddly ritualistic actions within Abilities to feel out the future.<br /> <br /> Look at their Bureaucracy and Medicine Charms; there's not really any generic &quot;manipulate destiny to do bureaucracy or healing stuff&quot; there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it also completely lacks ways to apply itself to things like crafting and lore, while in other areas like medicine its applications are limited to maybe one thing</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, even though it's been said that one might extrapolate Intelligence Charms to include ideas like being able to make cool stuff with less than one would expect, I'd still kind of assume that part of the point of Attribute Charms is being freed of the need to have the motifs of the Exalt apply equally to all areas.<br /> <br /> Even before we consider stuff like how even Solars are now being explicitly designed around an understanding that there isn't an equality between their Charms, albeit modeled in an evocative and intuitive (and hopefully consistent) manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands, though, I'm not sure I can even say Lunars should exist as Exalted at all, if their theme can't support everything an Exalt needs to be capable of doing.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:no-such-thing-as-generic-exalted-competency\" target=\"_blank\">Every what now?</a><br /> <br /> (Also has a nice summary of what I greatly expect Lunars to have Charms to be, ensconced within imagery of physicality and transformation and being unstoppable and terrifying, which need not always be conveyed by turning into an animal in whole or in part).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-04-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:07:54-07:00","id":105726,"title":"","content":"Exalted don't &quot;need&quot; to be capable of covering every base if they go off on paths that Solars can't access. Solars don't teleport, but Sidereals can. Conversely, Sidereals don't use most Abilities for the purposes that they were intended to cover when it comes to magic.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, they get monstrous and outright inhuman capabilities like the quickest healing in the setting, turning into daikaijuu or swarms of small animals, being able to reanimate corpses with magical larvae and other freakish capacities. Some capacities that they share with Solars are accomplished through the overarching theme of being feral, vicious, mysterious, seductive or fascinating. Luna has a general focus on storytelling, too, likely in a trickster's capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:17:29-07:00","id":105735,"title":"","content":"I would like it if Lunars had Charms that let them affect people's dreams, able to send nightmares or hold dream world conferences, which would be a great way that Lunars could keep in communication and coordinated with each other despite the vast distances across Creation they would be scattered over. It'd further show independence from infrastructure and dreams and nightmares have always had a connection with the symbology of the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:20:13-07:00","id":105737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105726#post105726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted don't &quot;need&quot; to be capable of covering every base if they go off on paths that Solars can't access. Solars don't teleport, but Sidereals can. Conversely, Sidereals don't use most Abilities for the purposes that they were intended to cover when it comes to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every type of Exalt should be able to do everything the others can (of course more or less difficult and by other means to the same goal). At least all Celestial Exalts. Because every Exalt is also suppossed to be a playable character. And hard limits forcing you to never be able to reach something... that's stupid.<br /> For example: Why should a Essence 5 Solar be able to use Solar Circle Sorcery, but not a Essence 8 Lunar? Why should a Solar never be able to change his shape while Lunars and Infernals do? Why can't Sidereals invent their own Charms (seriously, major flaw!)?<br /> Setting outright limits to what an Exalt can do in the long term is not helpful or balancing. You could balance that SCS issue for example by not letting your Lunars reach Essence 8 in the game, or at least not that easily.<br /> <br /> The most insane thing? Those 60 Exalts of the Eclipse Caste CAN do all these things. Of course Charmshare is broken, but what about Charm adoptation?<br /> <br /> That all being said, I'd really like something like Primordial Principle Emulation for Lunars, but with different mechanics and different targets. I want the Lunar to grow like an organism, to adapt, to evolve. Maybe this means copying some Solar Charms. Maybe I want basic astrology. All that should be possible. It should not be easy and it should not be gamebreaking. But something like that should always exist as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:34:09-07:00","id":105746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105737#post105737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every type of Exalt should be able to do everything the others can (of course more or less difficult and by other means to the same goal). At least all Celestial Exalts. Because every Exalt is also suppossed to be a playable character. And hard limits forcing you to never be able to reach something... that's stupid.<br /> For example: Why should a Essence 5 Solar be able to use Solar Circle Sorcery, but not a Essence 8 Lunar? Why should a Solar never be able to change his shape while Lunars and Infernals do? Why can't Sidereals invent their own Charms (seriously, major flaw!)?<br /> Setting outright limits to what an Exalt can do in the long term is not helpful or balancing. You could balance that SCS issue for example by not letting your Lunars reach Essence 8 in the game, or at least not that easily.<br /> <br /> The most insane thing? Those 60 Exalts of the Eclipse Caste CAN do all these things. Of course Charmshare is broken, but what about Charm adoptation?<br /> <br /> That all being said, I'd really like something like Primordial Principle Emulation for Lunars, but with different mechanics and different targets. I want the Lunar to grow like an organism, to adapt, to evolve. Maybe this means copying some Solar Charms. Maybe I want basic astrology. All that should be possible. It should not be easy and it should not be gamebreaking. But something like that should always exist as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a rather boring development. Everything would play mostly the same, The word we've gotten from the lead staff was that they're pushing away from completest omnicompetence because of how it ends up. Eclipses are also getting inverted, so that they can learn a small number of designated Charms from other sources but generally don't have the capacity to learn other Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:45:04-07:00","id":105756,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with that is, ultimately, is that it is <i>boring</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh look, Ted's glowing silver, that means he has to wait three extra Essence to be able to do the unique, mind-bending feats that Steve can do, while Steve glows gold, and that means he has to wait three extra Essence to be able to delve into the unique, protean feats that Ted can do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pfeh. At that point, why don't you simply remove the limitations on all Exalted, and just offer up all their powers as a grab-bag?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:02:40-07:00","id":105768,"title":"","content":"As far as we know, E6+ is not more powerful than E5 and below. It's more specialized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:48:40-07:00","id":105802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105737#post105737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every type of Exalt should be able to do everything the others can (of course more or less difficult and by other means to the same goal). At least all Celestial Exalts. Because every Exalt is also suppossed to be a playable character. And hard limits forcing you to never be able to reach something... that's stupid.<br /> For example: Why should a Essence 5 Solar be able to use Solar Circle Sorcery, but not a Essence 8 Lunar? Why should a Solar never be able to change his shape while Lunars and Infernals do? Why can't Sidereals invent their own Charms (seriously, major flaw!)?<br /> Setting outright limits to what an Exalt can do in the long term is not helpful or balancing. You could balance that SCS issue for example by not letting your Lunars reach Essence 8 in the game, or at least not that easily.<br /> <br /> The most insane thing? Those 60 Exalts of the Eclipse Caste CAN do all these things. Of course Charmshare is broken, but what about Charm adoptation?<br /> <br /> That all being said, I'd really like something like Primordial Principle Emulation for Lunars, but with different mechanics and different targets. I want the Lunar to grow like an organism, to adapt, to evolve. Maybe this means copying some Solar Charms. Maybe I want basic astrology. All that should be possible. It should not be easy and it should not be gamebreaking. But something like that should always exist as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the issue of sorcery, at least, I believe there are ingame artifacts in Second Edition to let Sidereals and Lunars learn Adamant Circle sorcery. It was implied in the White Treatise and MOEP Lunars that the Adamant Circle was not originally limited to Solars, but that the first-age Solars had used some kind of Working to keep it to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:28:22-07:00","id":105826,"title":"","content":"scary nightmare werewolf shit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:28:22-07:00","id":105827,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was also implied that Lunars invented Sorcery, Necromancy, and were the greatest Martial Artists and Artificers in the universe before The Man held them down. It's also a load of out-of-game horseshit.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you haven't noticed (And I'm guessing you either haven't, or don't care), a lot of the supposed 'things' the Lunar Exalted were the inventors of, or the supposed 'best' at, or 'We could <i>totally</i> do this before xyz', happens to be things limited to other Exalted types, and that they make in-character claims of having been stolen from the Lunars, with exactly <i>zero out-of-character backup</i>. Hell, it's even been explicitly called out as lies and wishful thinking by writers for the line, including the guy who wrote the damn book in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":374,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","user":"Nocte ex Mortis","date":". 04-04-2014, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:41:46-07:00","id":105837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105827#post105827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it was also implied that Lunars invented Sorcery, Necromancy, and were the greatest Martial Artists and Artificers in the universe before The Man held them down. It's also a load of out-of-game horseshit.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you haven't noticed (And I'm guessing you either haven't, or don't care), a lot of the supposed 'things' the Lunar Exalted were the inventors of, or the supposed 'best' at, or 'We could <i>totally</i> do this before xyz', happens to be things limited to other Exalted types, and that they make in-character claims of having been stolen from the Lunars, with exactly <i>zero out-of-character backup</i>. Hell, it's even been explicitly called out as lies and wishful thinking by writers for the line, including the guy who wrote the damn book in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno I really like the idea of Lunars and their unique position of between Worlds, their impermanence, having a large hand in the creation of the methods to shaping Creation and power over the dead/Underworld. Moreso with the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:43:18-07:00","id":105838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105827#post105827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it was also implied that Lunars invented Sorcery, Necromancy, and were the greatest Martial Artists and Artificers in the universe before The Man held them down. It's also a load of out-of-game horseshit.<br /> <br /> Edit: If you haven't noticed (And I'm guessing you either haven't, or don't care), a lot of the supposed 'things' the Lunar Exalted were the inventors of, or the supposed 'best' at, or 'We could <i>totally</i> do this before xyz', happens to be things limited to other Exalted types, and that they make in-character claims of having been stolen from the Lunars, with exactly <i>zero out-of-character backup</i>. Hell, it's even been explicitly called out as lies and wishful thinking by writers for the line, including the guy who wrote the damn book in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'd kinda prefer if you stuck to your pledge not to respond to me again. But if you're going to be responding it'd be nice to have some specifics instead of just &quot;a lot of the stuff&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:51:33-07:00","id":105842,"title":"","content":"I told you I would not reply to you on that thread again. I did not say that I would not reply to your attempts to spread wrong information elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The Lunars claim to have invented: Martial Arts, Sorcery (Specifically Solar Circle), Necromancy, Exalted Artifice, to have been the 'real power behind the thrones of the Solar Exalted', among other things. They also claim that the other Exalted stole their abilities with these things away, and in many cases used magic to permanently limit their access to them ever again. These have all been called out as <i>lies and wishful thinking</i> by the line writers and the developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:53:48-07:00","id":105846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105837#post105837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno I really like the idea of Lunars and their unique position of between Worlds, their impermanence, having a large hand in the creation of the methods to shaping Creation and power over the dead/Underworld. Moreso with the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordials invented Sorcery. Seriously, since the core rulebook of 1E, this has been the case. Necromancy was a joint effort between the Solar, Sidereal, and Lunar Exalted in going down into the Underworld, and <i>cracking open the tombs of the Neverborn</i> to get at their secrets. This had unintended consequences, like, say, everything that's happening in the Underworld right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:06:42-07:00","id":105855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105842#post105842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I told you I would not reply to you on that thread again. I did not say that I would not reply to your attempts to spread wrong information elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What you actually said was, &quot;I will not be replying to you on this again,&quot; which I took to mean the subject of Lunars. I'm not sure I actually want you to reply to my comments on any subject.</li> <li>You have no right to accuse me of attempting to spread misinformation.</li> </ol><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105842#post105842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars claim to have invented: Martial Arts, Sorcery (Specifically Solar Circle), Necromancy, Exalted Artifice, to have been the 'real power behind the thrones of the Solar Exalted', among other things. They also claim that the other Exalted stole their abilities with these things away, and in many cases used magic to permanently limit their access to them ever again. These have all been called out as <i>lies and wishful thinking</i> by the line writers and the developers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it would be more helpful to provide some specifics beyond &quot;writers&quot; and &quot;developers&quot; and &quot;the guy who wrote the book&quot;. Not even sure which book you mean; both of the books I mentioned were written by several people. Some quotes about sorcery would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:11:07-07:00","id":105858,"title":"","content":"No, I quite do have grounds to accuse you of spreading misinformation, as you have been doing so.<br /> <br /> As for your demands, why don't you pony up for once, and present your side, instead of accusing various people of lying and misrepresenting your position, when we call you out on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:18:04-07:00","id":105861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105846#post105846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordials invented Sorcery. Seriously, since the core rulebook of 1E, this has been the case. Necromancy was a joint effort between the Solar, Sidereal, and Lunar Exalted in going down into the Underworld, and <i>cracking open the tombs of the Neverborn</i> to get at their secrets. This had unintended consequences, like, say, everything that's happening in the Underworld right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I read the account of the Black Nadir Concordat, but I don't think the Sidereals had a hand in it.<br /> <br /> I also recall comments late in the line from at least a couple of writers (I can't remember who, or if any of the EX3 team are among their number) that Lunars actually had a knack for it. The sentiment was that restricting them to Shadowlands Circle was probably an error committed in pursuit of symmetry for symmetry's sake, and the writers in question would agree with giving Lunars access to the Labyrinth Circle. Always felt right to me, even aside the BNC. Kinda curious if/how that might be reflected in EX3's execution of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:30:24-07:00","id":105869,"title":"","content":"For consideration:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know if you're familiar with professional wrestling, but for such a lowbrow thing it has a very, very highly evolved lingo for describing story-building techniques within a complex milieu, which has proven very useful to me over the years. One of the pro wrestling concepts is that of 'building heat' i.e. generating interest in and support of a character with the audience. There are a number of ways of going about this. The most common, and by far the worst, is to steal heat from someone else. For example, you bring a relatively new guy out and have him beat the snot out of one of your established stars. If you are <i>very lucky</i> this builds heat for the new guy without hurting the old star too badly. More often it's seem as the cheap manipulation it is, and it just makes everyone involved look bad.<br /> Good heat-building methods usually take longer and involve an established property 'giving the rub' to the guy the company is trying to 'push'\u2014rather than just having the undercard guy go clown an established name, you have him start hanging around with the bigger guys, maybe tag-teaming with them, put them in some three-way matches where they're not carrying all the weight. By association with bigger names, some star power rubs off, and the transition isn't jarring. When they finally beat one of the bigger names, it seems like they've arrived where they ought to be.<br /> In other words, you've elevated one of your properties without losing anything. This is better than building up one of your properties at the expense of another.<br /> Lunars have primarily been given cheap heat throughout 2e\u2014they blame the Solars for holding them down, they claim they invented sorcery, they claim Solars stole this, stole that, held them back. They're secretly responsible for Chiaroscuro. Etc. This tarnishes the Solars and makes the Lunars look like crap, because no, we don't actually buy that they're as big as they're trying to act.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:37:49-07:00","id":105875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105858#post105858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I quite do have grounds to accuse you of spreading misinformation, as you have been doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, such as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105858#post105858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your demands</div> </div> </div> </div>...demands?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105858#post105858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why don't you pony up for once, and present your side..., instead of accusing various people of lying and misrepresenting your position, when we call you out on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT argument? I just mentioned that something was implied in a couple of the books, and you seemed to agree that it was, but said some writers have said it was more lies and wishful thinking. And I asked you what writers, and asked for some specific quotes, and now you refuse to say who it was and won't give any more detailed in formation until I present my side? My side of what? This is not an argument. I'm asking you for some more specifics in regards to what you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:50:14-07:00","id":105880,"title":"","content":"Dammit, surely eleven basic Charm ideas is not my limit... Glob knows that this thread desperately needs more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T16:01:30-07:00","id":105887,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhh I remember now...<br /> <br /> It took me a while, because unfortunately it's part of a thread now lost to us, and doesn't appear to have been put in the Chancel Aleph archive, but there was this great time when Holden pointed out that the stuff in Second Edition talking about how Lunars invented Sorcery and had the highest Circles of it and Martial Arts was part of a wider pattern of making the Lunars look like <i>petulant whingers</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not a good idea; it makes it hard to make them look impressive, or endear people to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T16:10:51-07:00","id":105893,"title":"","content":"As for what I'd like Lunar's to be able to do, here are a few examples of the flavor of their shape shifting blending with charm effects:<br /> <br /> <b>Telling of the Blood's Tale:</b> The lunar, upon consuming the blood of a hunted target, can internalize a memory they correctly suspect a target has. (Pretty much a refluffed Theft of Memory, since I don't think we will recognize the form Sorcery takes in 3E)<br /> <b>Transitive Property of Shape:</b> Because all forms the Lunars possess are one and the same being, a Lunar invoking this charm can alter their presence within a targets memory to appear as another shape within their heart's blood library. This could be used upon a sleeping target to invoke nightmares of the freezing vagabond they left out in the elements.<br /> <b>One With the Moon Method: </b>The Lunar can enhance any artifact composed of Moonsilver with their own Protean grace. A lunar may apply shape bending benefits to that of their panoply, such as enlarging a daiklave to the height of a sky-scraper, reinforcing their armor with a layered carapace, etc. (To be a little more specific on this one, I'd like to see are effects that can increase attack range without making extendable limbs the only flavor, especially when you consider how retarded that looks with archery weapons. The same charm may even allow for elemental damage to be add)<br /> <b>One With the Earth Method:</b> The Lunar learns to channel their fluid nature into creation, allowing them to change an area of non-magical material into other non-magical material with as little or as much change to the visual appearance as desired. The fortress's fate was sealed when the unsuspecting woodsman turned the flank of their hardened walls into the supple composition of down pillows.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T16:22:34-07:00","id":105895,"title":"","content":"As this is a &quot;what should Lunars able to do&quot; and not &quot;what does the MoEP: Lunars say that Lunars can do?&quot; thread, much of the latter shouldn't be posted. No Wyld Charms, no illusions, no copies of crafting Charms used by other Exalted, no really impressive organizational influence for general use that reaches farther off than reasonably possible (though even Solars are getting cut back on that point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:11:15-07:00","id":105911,"title":"","content":"Mind-Blanking Terror Technique should really be turned into what it sounds like: the Lunacy of the Uratha (Delirium in WtA, I think) where you radiate such monstrous fear that onlookers simply can't <i>process</i> you and eventually forget what they truly saw.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I like the <i>idea</i> (and name) of Labyrinth of the Beast, but it needs some dignity. So, instead of becoming a &quot;simple animal,&quot; it should transform the Lunar's mind into that of some primeval god-monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:23:54-07:00","id":105918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105911#post105911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind-Blanking Terror Technique should really be turned into what it sounds like: the Lunacy of the Uratha (Delirium in WtA, I think) where you radiate such monstrous fear that onlookers simply can't <i>process</i> you and eventually forget what they truly saw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain that it was there in 1e due to the Delirium from W:TA. It fits even better as Apocalypse-inspired, given that Lunars have been terrorizing the Threshold and the Realm for a good long while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, I like the <i>idea</i> (and name) of Labyrinth of the Beast, but it needs some dignity. So, instead of becoming a &quot;simple animal,&quot; it should transform the Lunar's mind into that of some primeval god-monster. </div> </div> </div>There were Alchemical Charms that already showed what it would be like if it were cleaned up for 2e. Abstract Abacus Implant comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:45:57-07:00","id":105932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105735#post105735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like it if Lunars had Charms that let them affect people's dreams, able to send nightmares or hold dream world conferences, which would be a great way that Lunars could keep in communication and coordinated with each other despite the vast distances across Creation they would be scattered over. It'd further show independence from infrastructure and dreams and nightmares have always had a connection with the symbology of the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent idea.<br /> In the last 2 books, there were plenty of good charms for Lunars in combat, and a fair amount when it came to social-fu, but their mental charms were pretty weak and lacking. I think No Moons are definitely the weakest Caste. So they kind of need some thematic resonance on which you can build that. And dream-based stuff seems like a good thematic base for that. They already have a charm for giving people nightmares, so the space is already there.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see them keep their Wyld-based stuff, and perhaps expand on it. Luna is the Goddess that controls and influences the Wyld, as opposed to the Sun's more aggressive stance. So I don't want to see them using Wyld-Shaping to destroy the Wyld like Solars, but influencing it, making it flow back and forth, that's got mileage.<br /> <br /> Another way to mine themes from the Moon for their mental charms, would be madness. Luna is the goddess of madness, the moon is associated with lunacy, etc. So charms which inflict or cure madness could fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:08:13-07:00","id":105947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105918#post105918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain that it was there in 1e due to the Delirium from W:TA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked it up, and <i>yeah</i>. Apparently, it only worked in warform, which is pretty stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105932#post105932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna is the goddess of madness, the moon is associated with lunacy, etc. So charms which inflict or cure madness could fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;To grant your wish, I will have to fill you with the energy of a thousand partying demons. You will become so overloaded with party energy that you'll demolish everything in your path!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T20:34:27-07:00","id":106003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105666#post105666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see some healing Charms that branch off from Halting the Scarlet Flow, allowing a Lunar to feed someone their blood like it was a burning hot panacea.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I have always hated this idea.<br /> <br /> If Lunar swordsmen can apply Lunar Charms to swordsmanship (ie: still get use out of their Melee ratings when employing Charms like Impressions of Strength), then why should Lunar physicians find their Medicine ratings irrelevant to their healing Charms?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the swordsman who relies on the grace and power of his limbs continues to do so as a Lunar, but why should the perceptive and intelligent physician find those faculties less applicable to supernatural healthcare than the robustness of his own health?<br /> <br /> If Lunars are going to approach Attributes as Sidereals approach Abilities, be consistent about it by putting weird and counter-intuitive tricks everywhere. Do NOT make &quot;Medicine&quot; Charms the sole exception.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals get away with this because their Charm progression crosses Attribute lines frequently, especially between a Charm and its own submodules; also, Alchemicals have problems holding all of their Charms at once, so I'm willing to accept their self-regeneration power having the potential to heal others. Especially since they have a more effective set of Medicine-action enhancers in the more heavily-Mental side of their Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-04-2014, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T20:54:00-07:00","id":106009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106003#post106003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I have always hated this idea.<br /> <br /> If Lunar swordsmen can apply Lunar Charms to swordsmanship (ie: still get use out of their Melee ratings when employing Charms like Impressions of Strength), then why should Lunar physicians find their Medicine ratings irrelevant to their healing Charms?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the swordsman who relies on the grace and power of his limbs continues to do so as a Lunar, but why should the perceptive and intelligent physician find those faculties less applicable to supernatural healthcare than the robustness of his own health?<br /> <br /> If Lunars are going to approach Attributes as Sidereals approach Abilities, be consistent about it by putting weird and counter-intuitive tricks everywhere. Do NOT make &quot;Medicine&quot; Charms the sole exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't expect it would be the sole exception. Perhaps if it's treated as more of a supplement? A Lunar who just plops it in there will see <i>some</i> benefit, but a Lunar physician will see the effects of his poultices and medicines magnified to a great degree by the additive.<br /> <br /> Though I suspect it would be nearer the latter, in that different Attributes can help in different ways, some less direct than others. I mean, in The MG's example, we're talking about a Lunar healing Charm in <i>Stamina</i>. There could certainly be other things in other Attributes: Dexterity could help with precision suturing, Perception would probably be fantastic in diagnosis, etc. Though even sticking to Stamina has other perks. A Lunar physician with some take on Scorpion &amp; Toad stuff can excrete stuff with medicinal benefits or that can be processed for such benefits. The same Charm cascade might be a Lunar assassin's/warrior's go-to for toxins. It might just be the nature of Stamina to be kind of indirectly beneficial to a host of areas.<br /> <br /> Bleggh, should probably sleep -_- Post feels kinda incoherent... Maybe patch up tomorrow. Yesssss","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T22:33:41-07:00","id":106052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105702#post105702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought this up in the other Lunars thread, though it got buried under a fresh wave of lapidary minutiae.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the core conceptual issue that their theme cannot be applied reasonably to all areas of character competence.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the theme of &quot;shapeshifting into animals and creatures of legend&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> First of all, as you say, shapeshifting into animals <i>isn't</i> their theme; it's their tool. It is an outgrowth of their theme rather than the center of it.<br /> <br /> Second of all, Lunars do not shapeshift into legendary beasts. They <i>are</i> legends who shapeshift into beasts; the mythic might originates from the Lunar, even in the form of Gaia's humblest creatures.<br /> <br /> A No Moon might kill and become a Nemean Lion, but a Full Moon in the form of an average member of panthera leo becomes the equal or superior to that great monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shapeshifting is an extremely broad tool, to be certain, but it also completely lacks ways to apply itself to things like crafting and lore, while in other areas like medicine its applications are limited to maybe one thing. </div> </div> </div>Holden said that, yes, Lunars aren't likely to shapeshift to craft or repair machines, except maybe as part of stunts. Aside from that, he said, Lunars will have Intelligence Charms.<br /> <br /> Sometimes monsters are scary because they're <i>smart</i>. Lunars can be that smart, cunning, tool-using monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T22:34:32-07:00","id":106053,"title":"","content":"Doing doctor stuff is an Intelligence/Perception + Medicine roll, if want to be a No Moon Doctor and was told that Stamina has the best healing charm instead of any other Mental Attributes because &quot;tribal barbarian magic hur dur&quot; then I will be very......disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T03:20:13-07:00","id":106176,"title":"","content":"Are people disappointed that the best Sidereal healing Charm is in Archery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T03:37:19-07:00","id":106186,"title":"","content":"If that thing where your totem rearranges your Charm trees pans out, Medicine Charms being spread out all over wouldn't be so much of a problem.<br /> It would also solve the Stealth-in-Charisma thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106003#post106003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I have always hated this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the medicine, not the treatment. If anything, it would supplement <i>all</i> Medicine rolls directed towards the recipient, not just your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T03:37:59-07:00","id":106187,"title":"","content":"I feel as though Lunars should inflict dreams and nightmares largely as an after effect of seeing <i>them</i>. Not so much a psychic dream projection thing as being so beautiful or horrifying that they torment the sleeping moments of witnesses for days or weeks afterwards. Or possibly any sensory interaction with them; the sound of their voice, the feel of their fingers running along the back of your neck, the scent of them wafting along the wind.<br /> <br /> Maybe with an idea that a Lunar can put subtle nuances into whatever they're projecting themselves by that code particular responses or even messages into the resulting dreams.<br /> <br /> I've only just remembered, back when it was talked about in terms of errata, there was a sense of giving Lunars a fair number of Merged Charms. Like, that scarring thing, that was going to be available in Strength and Charisma, wasn't it? I presume that would have helped somewhat at getting further in to trees that weren't part of a favoured Attribute, as a way of easing the burden of the limited available ones to a Lunar; like, if there was a cool trick up in Charisma, but you didn't favor it, your Strength or Dexterity Charms could get you a fair way into the prerequisites.<br /> <br /> I wonder if that, or something similar, might be on the table. Perhaps it could inform this apparent idea of spirit shapes helping to inform the shape or progression of Charm cascades; like, one way it could work is by having Charms that are basically merged <i>if</i> the symbolism of the spirit shape suggests a measure of relatedness of an unconventional Attribute to a certain Charm.<br /> <br /> Like, I don't know, owls are erroneously considered wise, so maybe some Dexterity based attack Charms could also serve as prerequisites for Intelligence Charms and also let you buy them at favoured costs. Or for Perception Charms, since owls actually do have impressive senses. Or quite likely the other way around; an owl totem No Moon who is able to use their Intelligence or Perception Charms as prerequisites for certain attack Charms, without having to favor Strength or Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T05:55:44-07:00","id":106233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106187#post106187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though Lunars should inflict dreams and nightmares largely as an after effect of seeing <i>them</i>. Not so much a psychic dream projection thing as being so beautiful or horrifying that they torment the sleeping moments of witnesses for days or weeks afterwards. Or possibly any sensory interaction with them; the sound of their voice, the feel of their fingers running along the back of your neck, the scent of them wafting along the wind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradim didn't really specify beyond &quot;affect dreams,&quot; but yes, that sounds about right.<br /> <br /> The idea could also extend into <i>baku</i>-based dream eater Charms, where you kiss or bite a sleeping person to glean knowledge from their dreaming mind.<br /> ...Though it might be better to just have Charms for deriving knowledge from your stolen shapes, with Life of the Hummingbird for non-lethal applications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T07:37:00-07:00","id":106262,"title":"","content":"Something that just occurred to me: why are the Lunar stealth charms in Appearance about mental effects, illusions, hiding in crowds and stuff?<br /> Not that there's necessarily a lot wrong with that (though Clover Can't Be Found is awkward), but why not chameolonic skin? I know you can grow it with HBT, but that just gives you +2 on stealth checks. Changing the colour of your skin to fit whatever's behind you seems very appropriate, as a proper charm effect.<br /> <br /> Isator, while I agree with your general point about the thematic appropriateness of charms, and linking them together for certain spirit-shapes (which looks like it's going to be what they're going to try to do) I don't get your example. What's wrong with Owl totem guys just having their No Moon charms? Owls are ambush fighters, and the ambush charms are in Wits anyway. It's not like Owls are particularly famous for their ability to dodge things.<br /> <br /> I like this idea the writers suggested of linking charms so you could get some out-of-tree charms that were appropriate a lot, but honestly, as people tend to favour the attributes that fit the totem anyway in my experience, it's not a huge issue. Probably somewhat useful though... and of course, the whole charmset will be different in 3rd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:10:02-07:00","id":106272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106176#post106176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are people disappointed that the best Sidereal healing Charm is in Archery?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a dodging Charm in performance, an attack Charm in Lore, Medicine is for fighting the undead, Bureaucracy can turn gods into artifacts... As I said, Sidereals get away with that because it's not the sole exception, but rather part of a running theme.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly like it, but I have always taken that to mean that Sidereals are not to my tastes, rather than there being anything wrong with how Sidereals do things.<br /> <br /> If I have any serious problem against that Sidereal Archery Charm, it is that it is the <i>only</i> Sidereal Charm that allows them to cheat out of their limited Charmset by buying new submodules. I would think it preferable for each Sidereal Ability (or at least one per Caste) to have one Charm that allows submodules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106186#post106186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the medicine, not the treatment. If anything, it would supplement <i>all</i> Medicine rolls directed towards the recipient, not just your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind if Lunar Stamina allows you to share regenerative blood with someone to speed up their basic powers of recovery. Indeed, that would be cool.<br /> <br /> I just don't want Lunar Stamina Charms to be so good at healing what ails people that it becomes a mandatory choice for a Lunar physician, just as I do not want Deadly Beastman Transformation to be a mandatory choice for Lunar combatants.<br /> <br /> However, I may just have to deal with that, because Scorpion-and-Toad Assumption was cool, and still had undeveloped space in the realm of &quot;defeat a disease within your own immune system; produce the antibodies which can spread out and cure the plague&quot;. Assuming that a concept like &quot;antibodies&quot; can be acceptably mythic for Lunar Charmspace.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would also solve the Stealth-in-Charisma thing. </div> </div> </div>If this is meant to be a refutation of my claim that Lunar medicine is the only misplaced perk, I have some counter-arguments. Even if you did not mean to refute me, these points are important for clarifying the purpose of the &quot;Stealth-in-Charisma&quot; feature.<br /> <br /> First of all, I'm pretty sure that there will be at least one Lunar Dexterity Charm which helps with sneaking around unnoticed, if only as a side-benefit to its general purpose. (Because if you can use a crane's stance to balance on the leaf of a tree, I'm pretty sure you can walk across gravel without making a sound, or over a nest of fallen twigs without leaving a trail.)<br /> <br /> Second, Lunars are like Sidereals in that their legendary powers are expressed in more forms than Charms. The Solar padfoot who relied on (Dexterity + Stealth) needs to improve both Traits and buy Stealth Charms. The Lunar padfoot can freely acquire the form of a cat (if it was not already his Spirit Shape) to become literally padfooted (and small, and inconspicuous), on top of learning the aforementioned Dexterity Charm which provides benefits to sneaking around. Plus, the Solar can pay favored costs only for Stealth dots, but the Lunar could favor both Stealth and Dexterity.<br /> <br /> Third, we are told over and over that Lunars are all about being seen. The Stealth-in-Charisma is not for avoiding the notice of people as per (Dexterity + Stealth); it is for dealing with the attention of people who have already noticed you. In short, the Lunar who uses that Social Charm has either already failed his (Dexterity + Stealth) contest, or he didn't bother trying to hide in the first place. His legend is not of the sneak-thief who slips by unseen, but as the confidence man who blusters his way past the guards with his silver tongue; (Manipulation + Presence = &quot;I'm totally allowed to be here, officer. Honest.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that thing where your totem rearranges your Charm trees pans out, Medicine Charms being spread out all over wouldn't be so much of a problem. </div> </div> </div>I have some reservations about that concept.<br /> <br /> Let's say a Solar had a totem of &quot;swashbuckling pirate&quot;, which involves Sail and Melee. But for the purposes of this example, he's only bought Sail Charms and no Melee Charms thus far.<br /> <br /> As one possibility for totem tree-remapping, the Solar's totem allows him to append Solar Melee Charms to his personal progression of Solar Sail Charms.<br /> <br /> This does him absolutely no good. If he wants Solar Melee Charms, he wants to start at the beginning, because that is how Charm progression should be designed -- such that the starting Charms are desirable if not essential to the purposes for which you would put the Charms that follow it. Recall Arete-Driven Athletic Stride, the Essence 2 Solar Charm with the modest effect that requires the powers of previous Athletics running-Charms to become synergistically powerful.<br /> <br /> If the Charm trees are not designed such that you want to progress from beginning to end, I question the integrity of the Charmset's basic arrangement. It would seem designed to <i>punish</i> anyone who isn't using their totem to sequence-break. Worse, it would seem like a blanket invitation to return to First and Second Edition's problem of unnecessarily long lists of prerequisite Charms which are only tangentially related to the Charm you want at the end.<br /> <br /> On top of that, remapping Charms from other traits into the tree of which you have already invested doesn't help you progress through the tree in which you already invested. That is, the Solar swashbuckler-pirate can nab the Melee Charms he wants and avoid the undesirable prerequisites because of how many Sail Charms he's bought, but that didn't save him from having to buy low-end Sail Charms which were only tangentially related to the high-end Sail Charms he actually wanted. Given that his greater priority on Sail Charms means sailing is more central to his concept than swashbuckling, it doesn't make sense that he should be forced to progress less efficiently through Solar Sail than Solar Melee.<br /> <br /> The <i>other</i> possibility for totem tree-remapping is allowing the Solar swashbuckler-pirate to learn Melee Charms with his Sail Ability rating rather than his Melee Ability rating. I think we can agree that's a bad idea on the face of it. But further, if Melee is part of the Solar's totem, it's important enough to his character concept that he should not only favor the Ability, but already have dots in it. So there would be no need to append Melee Charms into his Sail trees.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I'm not saying that the developers and writers can't find a way to make this work. What I am saying is that the &quot;totem tree-remapping&quot; idea is a statement John Morke made a while ago, at a time when he made it clear that many of his ideas for mechanically implementing the Lunar Exalted were not set in stone. I am also saying that I imagine that he and the others have seen the very problems I have described above, and this might have by now persuaded them to find some other benefit for Lunar totems.<br /> <br /> Or else they found a solution based on possibilities which do not occur to me; and if they occur to anyone else, I would appreciate hearing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:59:49-07:00","id":106308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106262#post106262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that just occurred to me: why are the Lunar stealth charms in Appearance about mental effects, illusions, hiding in crowds and stuff?<br /> Not that there's necessarily a lot wrong with that (though Clover Can't Be Found is awkward), but why not chameolonic skin? I know you can grow it with HBT, but that just gives you +2 on stealth checks. Changing the colour of your skin to fit whatever's behind you seems very appropriate, as a proper charm effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lack of shapeshifting Charms under Appearance is just because actually changing the way you look is something you generally do with Knacks. <i>Chameleon</i> is only an Affliction, so a stackable or improved version of it resulting in something like GITS-style active camouflage could be made as an Abomination with ST approval. And you can (with maybe a stunt) change your skin color and appearance with Changing Plumage Mastery and/or HBR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:13:53-07:00","id":106312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105702#post105702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought this up in the other Lunars thread, though it got buried under a fresh wave of lapidary minutiae.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the core conceptual issue that their theme cannot be applied reasonably to all areas of character competence. By this I mean, Solars have the theme of &quot;superhuman excellence&quot;. All of their Charms are built by saying &quot;In what ways could you apply superhuman excellence to task X?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106052#post106052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite.<br /> <br /> First of all, as you say, shapeshifting into animals <i>isn't</i> their theme; it's their tool. It is an outgrowth of their theme rather than the center of it.<br /> <br /> Second of all, Lunars do not shapeshift into legendary beasts. They <i>are</i> legends who shapeshift into beasts; the mythic might originates from the Lunar, even in the form of Gaia's humblest creatures.<br /> <br /> A No Moon might kill and become a Nemean Lion, but a Full Moon in the form of an average member of panthera leo becomes the equal or superior to that great monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>+10.<br /> <br /> Flexibility is really what makes Lunars my favorite Exalt type. You always have multiple ways of approaching a given problem. Playing other types, it often feels like you're a hammer looking for a nail. Whereas Lunars are like the sonic screwdriver of the Exalted setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-05-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:16:10-07:00","id":106313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106308#post106308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the lack of shapeshifting Charms under Appearance is just because actually changing the way you look is something you generally do with Knacks. <i>Chameleon</i> is only an Affliction, so a stackable or improved version of it resulting in something like <b>GITS-style active camouflage could be made as an Abomination with ST approval.</b> And you can (with maybe a stunt) change your skin color and appearance with Changing Plumage Mastery and/or HBR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Few Storytellers would, because Optical Shroud exists as a Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:26:07-07:00","id":106324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106313#post106313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few Storytellers would, because Optical Shroud exists as a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello. I'm not going to argue with you over what most STs would allow because I don't have access to that knowledge, but if there are any STs who wouldn't allow an improved <i>chameleon,</i> I haven't played with them. Generally, anything that can be achieved by an Affliction can be improved as a Blight or Abomination. It's not as if you don't usually have better ways of sneaking as a Lunar anyway. If you're shapeshifted into something innocuous like a housefly, the rules are that you don't even need a stealth or larceny roll under normal circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-05-2014, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:02:21-07:00","id":106346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106324#post106324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hello. I'm not going to argue with you over what most STs would allow because I don't have access to that knowledge, but if there are any STs who wouldn't allow an improved <i>chameleon,</i> I haven't played with them. Generally, anything that can be achieved by an Affliction can be improved as a Blight or Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to the extent that it matches the capabilities of Optical Shroud, which is implied in your choosing to specify use of thermoptic camo from GITS. That would be far too much for a mutation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not as if you don't usually have better ways of sneaking as a Lunar anyway. If you're shapeshifted into something innocuous like a housefly, the rules are that you don't even need a stealth or larceny roll under normal circumstances. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call the sidebar on page 129 a set of rules exactly, more a list of suggestions. It says that small shapes can gain full cover bonuses for hiding behind small objects, that there might be a DV bonus, and that there might be some bonus successes in certain endeavors, but there was no mention of auto-sneaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:04:07-07:00","id":106348,"title":"","content":"Also, for the record:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105858#post105858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your demands, why don't you pony up for once, and present your side, <u>instead of accusing various people of lying and misrepresenting your position, </u>when we call you out on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never accused <u>anyone</u> of lying, or of intentionally misrepresenting me. If you can find any quotes where I have, post them. The closest I've ever got is saying someone misunderstood something, which actually does happen.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106346#post106346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call the sidebar on page 129 a set of rules exactly, more a list of suggestions. It says that small shapes can gain full cover bonuses for hiding behind small objects, that there might be a DV bonus, and that there might be some bonus successes in certain endeavors, but there was no mention of auto-sneaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I need to clarify. It says, &quot;In most cases, a Lunar disguising herself through shapechanging doesn\u2019t require a roll\u2014as near perfect it is, nobody usually suspects anything.&quot; So in most cases, there's no disguise (larceny) roll needed to pass for an ordinary housefly, for instance. Which in turn means that unless a guard is trying to keep houseflies out of someplace, you don't need a stealth roll to sneak past.<br /> <br /> Edit edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106346#post106346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to the extent that it matches the capabilities of Optical Shroud, which is implied in your choosing to specify use of thermoptic camo from GITS. That would be far too much for a mutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seriously not going to argue with you about this. I didn't even know Optical Shroud was a charm but I said in my first comment that improving <i>chameleon</i> would need ST approval. If you don't approve, you don't approve. I don't see the value in arguing over what a hypothetical ST might allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-05-2014, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:31:26-07:00","id":106374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106262#post106262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why not chameolonic skin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, there probably are some magics that could be conveyed through the idiom of your skin colouring and pattern conveying mood and temperament...<br /> <br /> I feel as though Lunar Appearance Charms could be focused somewhat in the actual mechanical purpose of Appearance.<br /> <br /> Which, hopefully, will be broader in the new Edition in the first place.<br /> <br /> It does leave me somewhat wondering what a <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7NwmEEPSwr8\" target=\"_blank\">cephalopod camouflage</a> Charm would go under; Stamina?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isator, while I agree with your general point about the thematic appropriateness of charms, and linking them together for certain spirit-shapes (which looks like it's going to be what they're going to try to do) I don't get your example. What's wrong with Owl totem guys just having their No Moon charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nothing, if the Lunar is a No Moon.<br /> <br /> If they're another Caste, want some Intelligence or Perception Charms, but don't want to favour one or the other of those Attributes, the using the spirit shape as a gateway to dip into them seems fairly useful.<br /> <br /> Likewise if a No Moon doesn't want to favour certain Attributes more suited to attack, but still wants some of the Charms in their own right, or to key off of the imagery of their totem.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I'm mildly attached to the idea that, in basic terms of their shapeshifting, Lunars might take a very un-romantic view of animals, depending a bit on their Caste; an owl might be your totem, but it's mostly just an owl, not any culturally extended ideas of an owl. The spiritual idea of it can come through in some of the unconventional paths through which a Lunar develops their power, which I feel could be a nice way to differentiate between an owl totemned Full or No Moon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like Owls are particularly famous for their ability to dodge things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not referenced dodging.<br /> <br /> Owls have a really powerful, precise, and sharp grip. Dexterity seems like the Attribute that would cover those qualities in attacking. A No Moon Lunar might want such Charms, and be uninterested in dodging, or anything else that comes with favouring it. So perhaps the No Moon can use their spirit shape as the basis for having some Perception Charms act as prerequisites to that one Dexterity Charm they want.<br /> <br /> That example even kind of follows the logic of what the animal actually does; they sight it first, measure it up, and then swoop down for the kill.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:39:48-07:00","id":106379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106374#post106374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does leave me somewhat wondering what a <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7NwmEEPSwr8\" target=\"_blank\">cephalopod camouflage</a> Charm would go under; Stamina?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not Appearance?<br /> <br /> And in case it needs further clarification, the effect I was talking about would be something like this:<br /> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/Gits-katsuragi-camouflage.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> or this: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/b86664e0ad3f48370f91d595d8beb1ee/tumblr_mh1paxnBcA1r8tyjfo1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> Not invisibility, just improved blending-in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:54:18-07:00","id":106384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106374#post106374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, there probably are some magics that could be conveyed through the idiom of your skin colouring and pattern conveying mood and temperament...<br /> <br /> I feel as though Lunar Appearance Charms could be focused somewhat in the actual mechanical purpose of Appearance.<br /> <br /> Which, hopefully, will be broader in the new Edition in the first place.<br /> <br /> It does leave me somewhat wondering what a <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7NwmEEPSwr8\" target=\"_blank\">cephalopod camouflage</a> Charm would go under; Stamina?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Wits in that case. It would seem to fit in well with spontaneous attempts to avoid being detected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:00:57-07:00","id":106386,"title":"","content":"Invisibility isn't that impressive - it's what, -2 external penalty to attack or defend against? Really, the biggest problem is that it makes it very easy to reestablish surprise, and if a fighter doesn't have a surprise negator he's screwed anyway. I'd be okay with it as an Abomination. True, there are Charms that grant that power, blah-blah, but really, just because there are Charms that let you do it doesn't mean it can't be done without an equivalent Charm. See, for instance, the ability to fly.<br /> <br /> I hope to see more of the Companion aspect of Lunars. I feel that Lunars should be at their strongest when aiding those they care for - my Head-Canon has the Breaking of the Castes as a consequence of losing their Solar Mates, because the whole bond was made for the purpose of anchoring their identity, like how Luna's is anchored in her Intimacy to Gaia. So, more Argent Muse, more Ferocious Guardian Beast, and more Bond powers.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are the best Soldiers because they can put aside their differences and work together; Sidereals are the best Advisors because they don't need you to listen, Solars are the best Leaders because they can overrule any objections - and Lunars should be the best Companions, because they are always what their loved ones need.<br /> <br /> In a fight, a Lunar should boost his Mate in every way; make her faster and stronger, defend her so that she can focus on the offence, weaken the enemy with underhanded tactics, distract them at critical moments, and when she needs rest take up the slack and carry on. Outside of a fight, the Lunar should be the best assistant his Mate could ever ask for; the Squire who always has what his Knight needs, the fearless and tireless Steed she rides, the Hawk who finds her enemies, the Wolf who runs them down, the Spy who knows what they think, Seducer who turns them against themselves, the Advisor who tells her what she needs to hear, the Scholar who knows what she needs to know, the Courtier who leads her supporters and the Loyal Opposition who pushes her to do her best...<br /> <br /> A Lunar should be a Solar's Best Friend, and even a single Bonded pair should give an experienced Wyld Hunt nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:13:48-07:00","id":106398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106272#post106272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I may just have to deal with that, because Scorpion-and-Toad Assumption was cool, and still had undeveloped space in the realm of &quot;defeat a disease within your own immune system; produce the antibodies which can spread out and cure the plague&quot;. Assuming that a concept like &quot;antibodies&quot; can be acceptably mythic for Lunar Charmspace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe not the exact terminology, but the <i>idea</i> is sound, even more so if the whole thing is fairly unpleasant for the patient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this is meant to be a refutation of my claim that Lunar medicine is the only misplaced perk, I have some counter-arguments. </div> </div> </div>Nah, I was just doing a callback to hippokrene's Lunar Stealth thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:41:13-07:00","id":106414,"title":"","content":"Oh, I want the option to choose my &quot;Mate&quot; (urrgh, that term still sound like some kind of rapist stalker tween novel) instead of &quot;Somewhere in Creation there is a Solar ready to UMI you into being his sex-toy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:40:29-07:00","id":106490,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Bond being more personal and particular to the Lunar in question, and more about characterising how the Lunar feels about the Solar rather than giving the Solar a direct line into their head, and how both of these have the capacity to let the Lunar Bond to the first Solar who is really compatible with them (with regards to how this can have a variety of forms and functions, such as rivalry stuff)...<br /> <br /> But I feel like the Lunar only Bonding when they say &quot;right, you're my Solar now&quot; is a bit too... mechanistic. I still like the mythological connotations of the Lunar encountering the Solar and something primal and ancient inside of them seeing and wanting the Solar (not necessarily in the first moment they lay eyes on them). That it's an attachment the Lunar doesn't necessarily understand.<br /> <br /> Not Twilight imprinting stuff, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:55:12-07:00","id":106499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106490#post106490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the Bond being more personal and particular to the Lunar in question, and more about characterising how the Lunar feels about the Solar rather than giving the Solar a direct line into their head, and how both of these have the capacity to let the Lunar Bond to the first Solar who is really compatible with them (with regards to how this can have a variety of forms and functions, such as rivalry stuff)...<br /> <br /> But I feel like the Lunar only Bonding when they say &quot;right, you're my Solar now&quot; is a bit too... mechanistic. I still like the mythological connotations of the Lunar encountering the Solar and something primal and ancient inside of them seeing and wanting the Solar (not necessarily in the first moment they lay eyes on them). That it's an attachment the Lunar doesn't necessarily understand.<br /> <br /> Not Twilight imprinting stuff, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just say that Solars and Lunars always bond when working together.<br /> <br /> The actual bond mechanics have never been used in any game I've played, but Solars and Lunars generally synergize very well, the formers being exceptionally good in their particular areas and the latters having the flexibility to cover other areas and to see that situations develop in ways that allow their Solars to excel, in a nice (Attribute + Ability) relationship.<br /> <br /> Uh, but riding animals? No. Seriously, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:33:12-07:00","id":106524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106386#post106386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invisibility isn't that impressive - it's what, -2 external penalty to attack or defend against? Really, the biggest problem is that it makes it very easy to reestablish surprise, and if a fighter doesn't have a surprise negator he's screwed anyway. I'd be okay with it as an Abomination. True, there are Charms that grant that power, blah-blah, but really, just because there are Charms that let you do it doesn't mean it can't be done without an equivalent Charm. See, for instance, the ability to fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms that do that tend to do more. Plasma Thruster Assembly, for example, can also enhance attacks, and grants far greater speeds than flight would alone. You don't get mid-air &quot;dashes&quot; with abominations, nor can you knock people down around you if you take off.<br /> <br /> In any case, there's another example of adaptive camo mechanics in Exalted. You can find it in the gunzosha armor and some similar suits. It's another two dice over what the affliction gives, as an equipment-based bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope to see more of the Companion aspect of Lunars. I feel that Lunars should be at their strongest when aiding those they care for - my Head-Canon has the Breaking of the Castes as a consequence of losing their Solar Mates, because the whole bond was made for the purpose of anchoring their identity, like how Luna's is anchored in her Intimacy to Gaia. So, more Argent Muse, more Ferocious Guardian Beast, and more Bond powers. </div> </div> </div>It'd be a bit of a mess to have another connection to Gaia with Lunar Exalted. The spirit shape already occupies that space. Additionally, Lunars changed from what they were into something else. Companionship is an after thought to striking back against a foe that's holding all of the cards and has considerable advantages over you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:39:03-07:00","id":106531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106386#post106386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invisibility isn't that impressive - it's what, -2 external penalty to attack or defend against?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you really want to make a purely mechanical argument for invisibility sucking, and focus that argument on attack/defense rather than stealth, this is like saying &quot;the difference between Dex 1 and Dex 5 isn't that big a deal&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:40:01-07:00","id":106532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106272#post106272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some reservations about that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, I dunno. I don't feel using hypothetical Solar archetypes to explore a counter-example is appropriate. With the structure of the game, Charms fall under various buckets depending on the splat. Solars have 25 Abilities, but Lunars have only 9 Attributes. Solars can thus get a lot more granular in the types of concepts they can create between Caste and Favored in that structure, where some Lunar concepts are going to fall through the cracks there. Particularly as Solars really have one end toward which they're working, representing the skills of the human character and the archetype in Favored/Caste Abilities: the two mostly go hand in glove, and cases where they don't feel like big exceptions. Lunars, by contrast, need to represent both the human attributes of the character and the particular capabilities/associations of the totem. I feel involving some form of relocating and discounting particular Charms is meant to help with this. Cases will arise in which Lunars with totems that don't lend themselves to particular Attributes (i.e. it doesn't suit the character concept for the character to have that in Caste or Favored) will still find particular stuff <i>within</i> those Attributes that fit the totem like a glove.<br /> <br /> Here's an example of where I see it helping. Consider the Scorpion &amp; Toad stuff, since I consider it among the least controversial Charm effects Lunars have; I don't think I've ever heard a complaint or argument about them in concept. Nor about their placement in Stamina. However, let's think about toads and scorpions themselves. They're not very tough or durable. There's really not much of anything about them that screams, &quot;Stamina!&quot; So Lunars who take such small poisonous creatures would probably be interested in Scorpion &amp; Toad stuff, but their precious Caste/Favored Attribute choices may have more important places to go for the concept than Stamina -- say we're talking swift and nimble Lunar assassins, where durability really isn't the aim at all.<br /> <br /> Despite it being so appropriate and important to their concept to pick up Scorpion &amp; Toad stuff (possibly a big reason they'd picked that totem at all) and not to pick up Stamina, they'd have to make the unpleasant choice to buy those Charms -- and buy up to them -- for out-of-Caste/-Favored cost or make Stamina one of their Favored/Caste Attributes after all and pay out-of-Caste/-Favored cost on whatever they'd wanted from the abandoned Attribute. With the totem playing a role, though, that player has the opportunity to find a more convenient place for the Scorpion &amp; Toad stuff in their own trees and -- even if they can't -- they still get to buy it at a discounted rate. This can take some or all of the sting out of running into such a situation.<br /> <br /> To respond to a point I don't think you quite made, but which I see arising, I would also disagree with the idea that such cases coming up at all is a result of a poorly executed/designed or otherwise undesirable Charm set. It seems a natural consequence of having such a relatively small number of broad Attribute buckets into which Charms can fall (relative to Abilities) and trying to capture an array of totem possibilities that spans the entirety of the animal kingdom, possibly including folkloric and symbolic associations. Certain effects appear in the Attributes they do based on a certain logic, but the possible totems are so varied that not all of their qualities will adhere to that logic, creating little hiccups which this totem solution is meant to address.<br /> <br /> That said, there is the possibility that this totem thing may not benefit every concept. If the only totemic Charms one can get are ensconced in one's Favored/Caste Attributes anyway, it may help with rejiggering where those Charms fall in the cascade, if that's even an option, but clearly isn't as big a benefit. This was the incentive to sequence-break with totems you mentioned. It could be a possible concern, but I also have three possible counter-arguments, and I suspect it's one or both of the latter two: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Depending on one's design goals, there may not actually be a problem. The dev attitude in retaining BP and XP was (very broadly) explained as wanting to help people play the concepts they want, with less prioritization for on-paper equivalency. Following this logic, if the end goal is just &quot;Lunar characters should get easy access to powers that suit their totems,&quot; then characters who can't get Charms that are normally outside their Favored/Caste choices don't need them, so it doesn't matter for the purposes of that goal. Makes me feel kind of uncomfortable, since I'm not totally sold on that, but eh. Fortunately, I also don't think this is it. Or at least not <i>all </i>of it.</li> <li>It was said to be a system of keywords and associations. Perhaps the plan is to spread those keywords widely enough (and in a sensible fashion) that it isn't actually possible for your Caste-and-Favored choices to fall on all of them. In this case, you will definitely have Charms that can benefit from it. Some of these Charms may not be ones you want for that concept, but I don't see how that's different from not wanting to use everything in a particular Ability/Attribute for your concept. If the actual Charms in question are bad, that's a different issue.</li> <li>We probably don't have a complete picture, here. Aside from further development thoughts in the interim, what we got from John a ways back might have just been a taste. Maybe totems do other things, too, that make it kind of irrelevant -- or at least much less important -- that some may get more Charms out of this than others. Or, as I've recently been inclined to think, perhaps the keywords he mentioned serve important purposes <i>beyond </i>just giving certain Lunars easier access to those Charms.* Sunder, you spelled this out at the end of your post so I'm under no delusion that this is something you haven't considered. Just stating it here for completeness.</li> </ol><br /> * My present pet theory runs to the tune of, &quot;The keywords he's talking about are the legacy of the Protean keyword: wearing physically/thematically relevant shapes when using those keyworded Charms gives an additional benefit.&quot; I wouldn't consider this a complete explanation,* but I do see it playing a heavy role.<br /> ** For one thing, characters usually have few reasons to dip into animal shapes for traditionally social pursuits and even fewer for traditionally mental ones. I mean, this is unless some of those Charms play up mystical associations more than has been previewed or the keyword-linked benefits really make up for it. I kinda hope they will (if my idea is even in the ballpark), but we can't yet say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T17:32:09-07:00","id":106626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106532#post106532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm, I dunno. I don't feel using hypothetical Solar archetypes to explore a counter-example is appropriate. With the structure of the game, Charms fall under various buckets depending on the splat. Solars have 25 Abilities, but Lunars have only 9 Attributes. Solars can thus get a lot more granular in the types of concepts they can create between Caste and Favored in that structure, where some Lunar concepts are going to fall through the cracks there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The keywords would seem to introduce more granularity.<br /> <br /> Besides, is it really any different if I use a Lunar an example?<br /> <br /> Let's assume four favored Attributes (including Caste Attributes) and one totemic keyword. One, rather than five, because four of those keywords would merely repeat the favored Attributes. So we have a wolf totem that is Strength, Dexterity, Stamina, Charisma and has &quot;Keen Senses&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...This is showing me that I clearly didn't put enough thought into my Solar example. Because this example would suggest that the Lunar is capable of buying Perception Charms at favored prices so long as they have the Keen Senses keyword. Things like Heightened Sense Method, but not things like Leaf-Falling Scrutiny or Riding the Secret Wind.<br /> <br /> None of which remotely requires or encourages anything like mixing and matching Charm progressions. But since that was proposed, I <i>had </i>to include that concept in my Solar example, so I didn't stop to check if that even made sense.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I have absolutely no problem with totemic keywords which allow you to buy a particular subclass of Charms at discount even if you don't favor their Attribute. I was only arguing against the Charm progression-breaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Particularly as Solars really have one end toward which they're working, representing the skills of the human character and the archetype in Favored/Caste Abilities: the two mostly go hand in glove, and cases where they don't feel like big exceptions. Lunars, by contrast, need to represent both the human attributes of the character and the particular capabilities/associations of the totem. </div> </div> </div>Why would the association keywords of the totem be something that can't be represented by human attributes?<br /> <br /> Totem keywords will relate to Lunar Charms, and Lunar Charms are concerned with &quot;mythic&quot; powers rather than National Geographic biological marvels like electrical generation or explosive acid reactions. While I fully admit that &quot;poisonous&quot; might be a keyword (though one which might apply metaphorically with some social Charms as well as literally with physical ones), I doubt that we'll see it get more inhuman than that. Most likely, the keywords will be along the lines of &quot;sharp, tough, clever, graceful, hungry&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's an example of where I see it helping. Consider the Scorpion &amp; Toad stuff, since I consider it among the least controversial Charm effects Lunars have; I don't think I've ever heard a complaint or argument about them in concept. Nor about their placement in Stamina. However, let's think about toads and scorpions themselves. They're not very tough or durable. There's really not much of anything about them that screams, &quot;Stamina!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Scorpions are probably very tough for arthropods. Certainly, they are covered in biological armor.<br /> <br /> As for toads, Stamina Charms emcompass more concepts than &quot;taking a hit&quot; (and a toad totem Lunar doesn't have to learn a single one of those, either). Hibernation and breeding, for example, are Stamina Charmspace. Plus, frogs totally do eat particular substances and process them inside their bodies to create toxins. Poison-resistance is a natural association for such creatures, as is the ability to eat anything without getting sick from it.<br /> <br /> Nevermind whether the association is true. Are wolves, owls or snakes particularly more wise than many animals? Are lions brave?<br /> <br /> A keyword system which allows a toad Lunar to buy certain Stamina Charms without having to favor Stamina is just fine. But the Charm progression-breaking idea is ludicrous; why would anyone want to learn Scorpion-and-Toad Mastery before the S-and-T Absolution/Immunity Charms that allows the Lunar to <i>survive </i>creating hazardous substances inside their own bodies? The Lunar should want to learn Charm trees starting from the beginning, just like anyone else.<br /> <br /> ...Well, anyone but Sidereals, but the Sidereal Charmset is weird like that. (That is, I could see someone wanting the Sidereal Performance dodge Charm without needing to buy the performance Performance Charms, but they're <i>supposed </i>to put up with crap like that. That's <i>why </i>the Charm isn't in Sidereal Dodge in the first place.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T17:43:27-07:00","id":106629,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm going to address the &quot;chameleon / invisibility&quot; issue:<br /> <br /> I don't expect anything like Optical Shroud to make it into the Lunar Charmset, and I'm sure that Clover Can't Be Found is doomed. Both effects directly prevent the Lunar from being seen, which directly contradicts what we've been told Lunar magic will do.<br /> <br /> If Stealth is Dodge, then Lunars have poor &quot;attention dodge&quot; Charms and instead rely on &quot;attention soak&quot; Charms. &quot;Oh, you see me? Fine, but I stand so proud and tall that you assume I must belong here, and I'm probably your boss's boss. Or else I bend and bow and avoid eye contact like a servant, so I must be beneath your august notice. Or I speak in the accent of your nation, so obviously I must be one of your countrymen (Scent of Nations Attitude).&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a social chameleon at work. Granted, there is room for more direct camouflage, I suppose. Pretending to be a statue, perhaps, by taking on the color and visual texture of stone. But nothing so much as <i>Ghost In The Shell</i> or <i>Predator </i>transparency, since at least a fake statue is obviously there to be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T17:46:54-07:00","id":106630,"title":"","content":"Chameleon skin doesn't contradict what we've been told Lunars can do.<br /> <br /> Making a Lunar hard to see is not the same thing as directly preventing them from being seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:24:15-07:00","id":106642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106630#post106630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chameleon skin doesn't contradict what we've been told Lunars can do.<br /> <br /> Making a Lunar hard to see is not the same thing as directly preventing them from being seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm pretty sure it's too similar to pass muster, and stops at &quot;you can definitely see me, but I'm good at looking like someone or something other than me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:48:30-07:00","id":106653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=105846#post105846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordials invented Sorcery. Seriously, since the core rulebook of 1E</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not even remotely true. The 1e core (and most of 1e's books on Sorcery) just said that Sorcery's origins were mysterious; the story of Brigid (which was explicitly denoted as mythological and not-necessarily-true) very ambiguously implied that a demon was <i>involved</i> in her becoming the First Sorcerer (for what that may or may not be worth and for whatever accuracy-value of 'first' may or may not apply), but it also implied that the Fair Folk were involved, that the Gods were involved, and so on, and it put them all on equal footing as supernatural aspects of the world she encountered in her journey that ultimately made her a Sorcerer. To the extent that 1e talked about &quot;Infernal Sorcery&quot;, it presented it as a distinct sort of magic from what Brigid used. (This is not necessarily a good way to go either, for a variety of reasons, but the implication I always got from 1e was that Brigid -- to the extent that she's a historical figure and not a general mythological account of something done by the Exalted -- really was the first character in the setting to use what we now call Sorcery, fullstop, which was assembled from aspects of all the existing magics in Creation, one in which the supernatural secrets of the Demon Princes were just one in a very long list of secrets she was exposed to in her travels.)<br /> <br /> This did not become &quot;the Yozis invented Sorcery&quot; until 2e in Infernals, when everything became about the Yozis 24-7. I would not expect it to remain canon in 3e, because it is <i>dumb dumb dumb</i>. I did not sign on to play a Twilight to use Yozi Magic; it was especially dumb to make Sorcery 'Yozi magic' <i>while introducing a splat for people who want to draw on the powers of the Yozis</i>. Every book on Sorcery has gone out of its way to imply that it was thematically neutral and to express the idea that Sorcery draws on the entire breadth of the setting.<br /> <br /> The story of Brigid, again (while I'm not sure it was ever necessary) went out of its way to show how she drew on every aspect of the setting to become the First Sorcerer, <i>including Fair Folk and the power of the Wyld, which predates the Yozis</i>. I'm not saying that out of a nit-picking desire to say 'well yes but when Infernals retconned that to &quot;the Yozis invented Sorcery lol&quot; they were contradicting line X of page Y of this book&quot; -- I'm not that fond of Brigid's story anyway, like I said -- but my point is that the fact that they had to contradict the fact that Brigid's journey touched on things outside the Yozis is a symptom of how aspects of late-2e narrowed the scope of the setting by making everything about the Yozis. Turning &quot;Mara was involved in Brigid's creation of Exalted Sorcery&quot; into &quot;Mara handed Brigid Sorcery, which is Yozi Magic, fully-formed as a plot by the Yozis, and oh yeah the rest of the story is unimportant&quot; belittles Sorcery and cheapens the Exalted in order to burnish some dumb handwavy NPCs. The core of the story of Brigid -- in my opinion, the only part of it that's really important or worthwhile -- is that Sorcery is derived from <i>everything</i> (a category which is not, despite what 2e would have you believe, limited to the conceptions or creations of the Yozi, as, again, the fact that Brigid had to study under one of the princes of the chaos beyond Creation along the way.) 2e narrowed and collapsed that grand mythology down to one line vaguely-implying Mara's involvement in the same way that it narrowed and collapsed large portions of the setting.<br /> <br /> Let me put it like this -- suppose you had a superhero, I don't know, Doctor Strange. And then one day you say &quot;Doctor Strange's magic is actually derived from GALACTUS! He is using the POWER COSMIC and never knew it!&quot; Do you think that fans of Doctor Strange would enjoy this revelation? Especially if they were people, like me, who thought Galactus was a pretty dumb kind of character in the first place and thought Doctor Strange was really cool? No, they would break out the torches-and-pitchforks. And if you told them that they should be happy that Doctor Strange was retconned to actually be using a facet of the Power Cosmic because the Power Cosmic is awesome and anyway why aren't they glad Doctor Strange is now connected to a much more powerful character -- someone who predates the universe! -- they would probably go murder-eyes.<br /> <br /> That is <i>exactly</i> what the retcon about the Yozis being the sole-direct-one-true-source-of-Sorcery did to Twilights. I am not exaggerating or speaking euphemistically or using it as an example, I am saying is exactly, down to a T, like saying that Doctor Strange's powers are actually derived from Galactus. It is that terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-05-2014, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:31:03-07:00","id":106667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106653#post106653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hyperbole... and lots of it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Look... I get that you're upset that the Yozi invented sorcery. I don't care, but I get it. Your reaction on the other hand is... ridiculous... at best... The thing that you don't understand is that in the end, it doesn't matter where Sorcery comes from. The Yozi have absolutely no ability to influence what you can learn, or do, with sorcery. They cannot determine how powerful of a sorcerer you can become, they cannot stop you from casting any spells, nor can they influence or taint the results. Your complaint is like bitching about the fact that you just found out that the Chinese invented gun powder before the Europeans. It's an interesting bit of trivia, but ultimately that fact is unimportant to our modern day understanding of firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:40:33-07:00","id":106670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106524#post106524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms that do that tend to do more. Plasma Thruster Assembly, for example, can also enhance attacks, and grants far greater speeds than flight would alone. You don't get mid-air &quot;dashes&quot; with abominations, nor can you knock people down around you if you take off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I said I wasn't going to argue with you about this particular piece of lapidary minutiae, but just for the record, having wings actually does allow you to make aerial dashes - you can dash using any kind of movement, even when climbing a rope. The wings themselves can also be used directly for unarmed attacks and synergize well with Lunar extra-attack charms. On top of that, there's at least one Martial Art style that exclusively uses attacks made with wings: Dagger Wind Style. It lets you fling out razor-edged currents of air that saw things apart at range. Wings are pretty useful things to have.<br /> <br /> Also, shifting mutations through Hybrid Body Rearrangement already lets Lunars do lots of things other Exalts need specific charms for, such as growing gills to breathe underwater... enhancing natural armor... producing weapons... parrying lethal unarmed... buffing parry DVs (<i>quills</i> mutation)... developing extra senses to see in the dark or detect invisible things... enhancing existing senses... converting their bodies to stone, fire etc... walking on ceilings... becoming invulnerable to heat and cold... instantly regrowing a severed limb (though without regaining health levels)... and... oh yeah... flying. &quot;A different kind of Exalt needs a charm to do that&quot; just seems like a strange reason not to let a player accomplish something using HBR. I mean there are things HBR enables that some Exalts can't do even with a charm. It's the one Knack that epitomizes Lunar awesomeness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106524#post106524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, there's another example of adaptive camo mechanics in Exalted. You can find it in the gunzosha armor and some similar suits. It's another two dice over what the affliction gives, as an equipment-based bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so that's +4 to stealth. Would that be too much for an Abomination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-05-2014, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T20:22:10-07:00","id":106681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106667#post106667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look... I get that you're upset that the Yozi invented sorcery. I don't care, but I get it. Your reaction on the other hand is... ridiculous... at best... The thing that you don't understand is that in the end, it doesn't matter where Sorcery comes from. The Yozi have absolutely no ability to influence what you can learn, or do, with sorcery. They cannot determine how powerful of a sorcerer you can become, they cannot stop you from casting any spells, nor can they influence or taint the results. Your complaint is like bitching about the fact that you just found out that the Chinese invented gun powder before the Europeans. It's an interesting bit of trivia, but ultimately that fact is unimportant to our modern day understanding of firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still cheapens the origin of it. Sorcery should be mysterious, with many possible origins with any of them true. I like the mythological Brigid, who may have not even existed. I rather think than this is how it's going to return to in 3E because the game isn't going to be Yozi focused anymore The Yozi are imprisoned, moving on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T20:37:36-07:00","id":106687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106642#post106642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm pretty sure it's too similar to pass muster, and stops at &quot;you can definitely see me, but I'm good at looking like someone or something other than me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea where you're getting this from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T20:57:57-07:00","id":106697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106670#post106670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realize I said I wasn't going to argue with you about this particular piece of lapidary minutiae,</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing lapidary here. Well, not unless we bring Crystal Polar mutants into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but just for the record, having wings actually does allow you to make aerial dashes - you can dash using any kind of movement, even when climbing a rope. The wings themselves can also be used directly for unarmed attacks and synergize well with Lunar extra-attack charms. On top of that, there's at least one Martial Art style that exclusively uses attacks made with wings: Dagger Wind Style. It lets you fling out razor-edged currents of air that saw things apart at range. Wings are pretty useful things to have. </div> </div> </div>And it's also very handy to travel at speeds in excess of 150 yards in one Move action, at DV -0. Or any of the other things that Plasma Thruster Assembly does, which is why it's an Essence 3 Charm and not an abomination. Though, having said abomination makes long-term flight a whole lot easier and discounts the mote cost, like how having spinnerets makes Argent Weaver Art free... but spinnerets is no substitution for Argent Weaver Art, as it taps out easily and its webs aren't as strong, among other limitations.<br /> <br /> There is a class of mutations that do manage to reach for that capacity, but they tend to be things that Exalted can't get, like Immortal Flesh or Alchemical Demiurge, the latter of which is more of a plot device than a power to be used for devastating effect, and one kept out of the hands of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, shifting mutations through Hybrid Body Rearrangement already lets Lunars do lots of things other Exalts need specific charms for, such as growing gills to breathe underwater... enhancing natural armor... producing weapons... parrying lethal unarmed... buffing parry DVs (<i>quills</i> mutation)... developing extra senses to see in the dark or detect invisible things... enhancing existing senses... converting their bodies to stone, fire etc... walking on ceilings... becoming invulnerable to heat and cold... instantly regrowing a severed limb (though without regaining health levels)... and... oh yeah... flying. &quot;A different kind of Exalt needs a charm to do that&quot; just seems like a strange reason not to let a player accomplish something using HBR. I mean there are things HBR enables that some Exalts can't do even with a charm. It's the one Knack that epitomizes Lunar awesomeness. </div> </div> </div>All of these things pale in comparison to Charms that do the same things. They're nice, modest bonuses, but they don't come close to serving as full substitutes. Also, Exalted can't get the Regeneration mutation, even with HBR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:00:17-07:00","id":106701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106667#post106667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look... I get that you're upset that the Yozi invented sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm upset that <i>2e retconned the Yozi into inventing Sorcery</i>. There's an extremely huge difference.<br /> <br /> (Again, it's the difference between saying &quot;I'm annoyed that this writer retconned Doctor Strange into having his powers derived from Galactus&quot; and &quot;I'm annoyed that the Silver Surfer uses the power of Galactus.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it doesn't matter where Sorcery comes from. The Yozi have absolutely no ability to influence what you can learn, or do, with sorcery. They cannot determine how powerful of a sorcerer you can become, they cannot stop you from casting any spells, nor can they influence or taint the results. Your complaint is like bitching about the fact that you just found out that the Chinese invented gun powder before the Europeans. It's an interesting bit of trivia, but ultimately that fact is unimportant to our modern day understanding of firearms. </div> </div> </div>It absolutely does matter, for the same reason it matters that Solars were once kings in a vanished age, or for the same reason it matters that the Sidereals held a great prophecy and changed the course of Creation based on what it said. These things define the character you're playing, even if they don't have direct mechanical impact.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation fundamentally defines what it means to be a Sidereal or a Dragon-Blooded, even if it took place 1500 years ago. I mean, you can ignore it, personally -- I'm sure plenty of Sidereals do; they have a lot of things to worry about -- but it's still a huge part of the setting's definition of them, and if you play a game it's likely to come up eventually. The First Age defines what it means to be a Solar -- again, you can totally have your Solar ignore it, but it fundamentally shapes the place of Solars in the setting.<br /> <br /> The origins of Sorcery (if the game is going to specify its origins) fundamentally define what it means to be a Sorcerer in a similar sense. It defines what Sorcery <i>is</i>, and through that, it defines a huge part of how the game approaches a certain kind of magic (and an entire genre of magic.) While I think that the story of Brigid was unnecessary, 1e's origin story for Sorcery was still basically broad enough and mysterious enough to support what I wanted. 2e's retconned Yozi-centric version of it was not. It makes the statement that all the vastly weird mystery of the supernatural that Sorcery gives you access to comes down to &quot;lol secrets of the Yozis.&quot; It says that when you initiate into Sorcery and begin exploring the cosmic sorcerous truths of the universe, you're just sorting through regurgitated Yozi-dreck. It says that, fundamentally -- speaking in the abstract here, in a sort of zoomed-out view of what Sorcery means --that the supernatural truth of Exalted <i>is the Yozis</i>, that if you boil down the deep secret understanding of the universe you get Malfeas' brainfarts.<br /> <br /> Exalted deserves better than that. Sorcery deserves better than that. The Yozis are vast and terrible, but the secret revealed supernatural truth of the universe deserves to be grander and broader and deeper than them. The Sorcerer needs to stand on its own as an archetype, and the fragments of knowledge a sorcerer stitches together into their spells should hint at a deeper, more holistic truth than just being the secrets of some mere has-been titans they defeated thousands of years ago.<br /> <br /> Demon-summoning should always be tempting, mind; the powers of Hell are totally an important part part of the vast supernatural tapestry that makes up Exalted, and therefore one of the many sources Sorcery should draw on. But it should just be one of many, and when you specify the lords of Hell as the ultimate origin by which Exalted learned the secrets of Sorcery, you're fundamentally changing the definition of what it means to be a sorcerer. If you don't see it, you might compare it to Necromancy -- unlike Sorcery, Necromancy <i>did</i> have an origin in 1e that explicitly said that it was the secrets of fallen titans. That was written in for a specific purpose -- to cast a specific sort of shadow over Necromancy, to give players an unsettling thrill when they draw on its spells, knowing that they're using forbidden powers ripped from the minds of dead gods. I don't know whether that's necessary for Necromancy in 3e, but it was distinct and served a particular purpose for Necromancy; Sorcery's origin, by comparison, was enigmatic, with only an allegorical myth of a supernatural journey, deliberately designed to be open to many interpretations.<br /> <br /> (Some people have pointed out that Brigid's story seems implausible in some respects; on reflection, I think that this was somewhat the point. Many real-life mystical or mythological traditions have that sort of allegorical journey in them -- I don't think it was meant to be read as literal in any respect.)<br /> <br /> Again, I don't think there's any danger that 3e will repeat that, because the authors have clearly indicated that they intend to tone down the Yozi-centric stuff that happened in late 2e, and 2e's retcon to the origin of Sorcery was one of the stupidest examples of that. I'm just arguing that it deserves to be tossed down the memory hole of dumb 2e shit that seemed like a good idea at the time but which we now blissfully pretend never happened. If you don't care, that's fine; I'm sure lots of people would say &quot;why do you care so much if some writer declared that Doctor Strange's powers are all derived from Galactus?&quot; I mean, yeah, it's a kinda geeky thing to care about.<br /> <br /> It's still stupid, though. To me, at least, it cuts at the core of what I consider to be cool about being a sorcerer, removing a huge part of the mysticism that makes them what they are and replacing it with <i>fucking Galactus</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:05:13-07:00","id":106703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106697#post106697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these things pale in comparison to Charms that do the same things. They're nice, modest bonuses, but they don't come close to serving as full substitutes. Also, Exalted can't get the Regeneration mutation, even with HBR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's talking about <i>regeneration?</i> <i>Multiple limbs</i> is an Abomination. Normally, it costs 4 motes to produce through HBR, and grows 2 arms. But if you only want to replace one you've lost, 2 motes should be sufficient.<br /> <br /> If you can shapeshift reflexively, you <i>should</i> be able to use <i>multiple heads</i> the same way... although your ST may call for a stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-06-2014, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:10:09-07:00","id":106704,"title":"","content":"I wonder what will ranged-combat Lunar look like, in Second Edition it's &quot;Use these charms for both closed and ranged attacks&quot; which is pretty boring, not to mention the charm's name and fluff kinda paint an impression of &quot;Attack from afar is dirty tactic, no true Barbarian will use it!&quot;. I mean, the Silver Huntress does take inspiration Artemis, right ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:23:39-07:00","id":106709,"title":"","content":"There was proto-errata that changed Wind-Wings Carry Technique. It never made it to official status, but it's not forgotten...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WIND-WINGS CARRY TECHNIQUE<br /> Cost: 1m+; Mins: Strength 2 Essence 2; Type: Reflexive (Step 1)<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK, Merged (Wits), Obvious<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Replace the text of the Charm with the following:<br /> Running and hiding are equally futile when Luna\u2019s Chosen are on the hunt. Phantom wings etched in wind or shadow briefly<br /> appear to speed along a projectile enhanced by this Charm, or to turn an attack\u2019s course suddenly to veer around cover.<br /> Each mote spent on this Charm adds (half the attack\u2019s range value) to the range of a projectile attack, or allows any<br /> form of attack to ignore one point of penalties due to the target being behind cover.<br /> Up to (Essence x 2) motes may be spent to enhance a single attack.<br /> <br /> At Essence 4+, each mote spent on this Charm extends a projectile\u2019s range and ignores one point of cover.<br /> <br /> Merged: An identical Charm also exists in Wits. </div> </div> </div>A pity that the forum crashed and took out some other alterations that Holden had posted. 1e had a Charm to ignore the Strength maximum of your bow, but as you can probably guess, it also had some problems. Like, you could accidentally break your bow using it if you messed up the activation roll. And the fact that it required an activation roll to function, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106703#post106703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's talking about <i>regeneration?</i> <i>Multiple limbs</i> is an Abomination. Normally, it costs 4 motes to produce through HBR, and grows 2 arms. But if you only want to replace one you've lost, 2 motes should be sufficient.<br /> <br /> If you can shapeshift reflexively, you <i>should</i> be able to use <i>multiple heads</i> the same way... although your ST may call for a stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the capabilities of your proposal on the grounds of it rather devaluing the healing Charms and DBT. It may not be a good setup, but I don't think the intention was to short-circuit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:29:48-07:00","id":106712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106709#post106709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the capabilities of your proposal on the grounds of it rather devaluing the healing Charms and DBT. It may not be a good setup, but I don't think the intention was to short-circuit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Producing <i>multiple limbs/heads</i> doesn't heal any actual health levels, at least not to my knowledge. You still need healing charms for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T23:41:22-07:00","id":106753,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm upset that <i>2e retconned the Yozi into inventing Sorcery</i>. There's an extremely huge difference.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">No, not really. It was never explained where sorcery came from, just that Brigid was the first exalt to learn of it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Again, it's the difference between saying &quot;I'm annoyed that this writer retconned Doctor Strange into having his powers derived from Galactus&quot; and &quot;I'm annoyed that the Silver Surfer uses the power of Galactus.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery is not \u201cthe power of the yozi\u201d, the fact that you don\u2019t know that makes me wonder just how much of your opinion is based on things that you have read, rather then just what you have heard...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It absolutely does matter, for the same reason it matters that Solars were once kings in a vanished age, or for the same reason it matters that the Sidereals held a great prophecy and changed the course of Creation based on what it said. These things define the character you're playing, even if they don't have direct mechanical impact.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Nope. Not even close. It has the same impact as telling a gun nut that gunpowder was invented by the Chinese, and since you can\u2019t seem to understand what that means I\u2019ll explain it to you. It means only what it means to that particular person. To some, it doesn\u2019t matter, to others, it\u2019s an interesting fact, but hardly important in comparison to everything that\u2019s come after, and to a vast minority, they blow it out of proportion and exaggerate it\u2019s meaning until it ruins it for them. Guess which one you are...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Usurpation fundamentally defines what it means to be a Sidereal or a Dragon-Blooded, even if it took place 1500 years ago. I mean, you can ignore it, personally -- I'm sure plenty of Sidereals do; they have a lot of things to worry about -- but it's still a huge part of the setting's definition of them, and if you play a game it's likely to come up eventually. The First Age defines what it means to be a Solar -- again, you can totally have your Solar ignore it, but it fundamentally shapes the place of Solars in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Totally irrelevant to the question of sorcery\u2019s origins, but I guess you do like to run on.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The origins of Sorcery (if the game is going to specify its origins) fundamentally define what it means to be a Sorcerer in a similar sense. It defines what Sorcery <i>is</i>, and through that, it defines a huge part of how the game approaches a certain kind of magic (and an entire genre of magic.)</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">So... the power to shape, create, and alter the very underpinnings of the world, should be completely different, separate from, and have no relation to, those that shaped, created, and altered the world and created the laws therein... Yeah... that makes sense...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While I think that the story of Brigid was unnecessary, 1e's origin story for Sorcery was still basically broad enough and mysterious enough to support what I wanted. 2e's retconned Yozi-centric version of it was not.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">And now we get to your real problem and why I can seem to care about it. It all comes down to whining about something that wasn\u2019t the flavor that you wanted, when it\u2019s mechanical and story impact of the thing was basically nil.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes the statement that all the vastly weird mystery of the supernatural that Sorcery gives you access to comes down to &quot;lol secrets of the Yozis.&quot; It says that when you initiate into Sorcery and begin exploring the cosmic sorcerous truths of the universe, you're just sorting through regurgitated Yozi-dreck. It says that, fundamentally -- speaking in the abstract here, in a sort of zoomed-out view of what Sorcery means --that the supernatural truth of Exalted <i>is the Yozis</i>, that if you boil down the deep secret understanding of the universe you get Malfeas' brainfarts.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The fact that you can take a concept as vast as \u201cThe power and knowledge by which all that is, came to be\u201d and reduce it to \u201clol secrets of the Yozis\u201d tells me much about your position, and mentality. I\u2019m guessing that you\u2019re an self-entitled solar player...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Exalted deserves better than that.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Called it...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery deserves better than that.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Better then being the power by which the world, and all therein it was shaped?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yozis are vast and terrible, but the secret revealed supernatural truth of the universe deserves to be grander and broader and deeper than them.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It is, and it\u2019s quite sad that you can\u2019t see that.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sorcerer needs to stand on its own as an archetype, and the fragments of knowledge a sorcerer stitches together into their spells should hint at a deeper, more holistic truth than just being the secrets of some mere has-been titans they defeated thousands of years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Chinese invented gunpowder, this does not make them the foremost experts on the matter today. If you can\u2019t see the relevance to this in regard to the subject then perhaps you need to bow out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon-summoning should always be tempting, mind; the powers of Hell are totally an important part part of the vast supernatural tapestry that makes up Exalted, and therefore one of the many sources Sorcery should draw on. But it should just be one of many, and when you specify the lords of Hell as the ultimate origin by which Exalted learned the secrets of Sorcery, you're fundamentally changing the definition of what it means to be a sorcerer. If you don't see it, you might compare it to Necromancy -- unlike Sorcery, Necromancy <i>did</i> have an origin in 1e that explicitly said that it was the secrets of fallen titans. That was written in for a specific purpose -- to cast a specific sort of shadow over Necromancy, to give players an unsettling thrill when they draw on its spells, knowing that they're using forbidden powers ripped from the minds of dead gods. I don't know whether that's necessary for Necromancy in 3e, but it was distinct and served a particular purpose for Necromancy; Sorcery's origin, by comparison, was enigmatic, with only an allegorical myth of a supernatural journey, deliberately designed to be open to many interpretations.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">(Some people have pointed out that Brigid's story seems implausible in some respects; on reflection, I think that this was somewhat the point. Many real-life mystical or mythological traditions have that sort of allegorical journey in them -- I don't think it was meant to be read as literal in any respect.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I feel that there is a fundamental lack of comprehension for the yozi\u2019s place in regard to 2e\u2019s sorcery on your part, so I\u2019m going to break it down for you. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Yozi did the following things with regard to sorcery in 2e:</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Discovered it (The rules were there first for them to discover)</li> <li>Found out that it was a universal means of essence manipulation and expression. (LIke math)</li> <li>Used it to build the world and all therein.</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Thought they would be clever and teach it to the exalted host. (nothing could </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">possibly go wrong)</span></li> <li>Taught it to Brigid.</li> <li>Tried to temp sorcerers into becoming akuma. (mostly failed)</li> <li>The end.</li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">That\u2019s it. You know... I think I have a better analogy for you. You are bitching about the fact that the Arabs discovered the concept of 0 first. Sorcery doesn\u2019t \u201cCome from\u201d the Yozi. It\u2019s not powered by them either. They just discovered it first, and you\u2019re throwing a bitch fit about it. Sorcery, and the underpinnings there of, existed before the Primordials, else how could they discover it...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I don't think there's any danger that 3e will repeat that, because the authors have clearly indicated that they intend to tone down the Yozi-centric stuff that happened in late 2e, and 2e's retcon to the origin of Sorcery was one of the stupidest examples of that. I'm just arguing that it deserves to be tossed down the memory hole of dumb 2e shit that seemed like a good idea at the time but which we now blissfully pretend never happened. If you don't care, that's fine; I'm sure lots of people would say &quot;why do you care so much if some writer declared that Doctor Strange's powers are all derived from Galactus?&quot; I mean, yeah, it's a kinda geeky thing to care about.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">You say geeky, I say stupid... Tomato tamato... Also, sorcery does not \u201ccome from the yozi\u201d it was taught to the exalted \u201cby\u201d the yozi. If you can\u2019t understand the difference, then you need to sit and reread the books... again...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still stupid, though. To me, at least, it cuts at the core of what I consider to be cool about being a sorcerer, removing a huge part of the mysticism that makes them what they are and replacing it with <i>fucking Galactus</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It all boils down to the fact that you are bitching about something that doesn\u2019t exist... You should feel bad...<br /> <br /> You're like those people who bitch about lilun being a child, ignoring the fact that while she may have been 10 when she was taken. She was taken over a decade ago. That would put her at 20+ years of age... not 10...</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 04-06-2014, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:31:13-07:00","id":106786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106753#post106753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff and stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to reply to each part individually, because that gets pretty hard to read real fast. But I'll reply to what I think seems to be the gist of your issues with what I said, or at the parts that seem interesting to me.<br /> <br /> I believe that the Sorcerer, as an archetype, is basically about esoteric wisdom -- about someone who sees the occult truth behind the way the world works, and who can manipulate it to their advantage. Anything that the books say about the source through which the Exalted acquired access to sorcery therefore makes a sweeping statement about the nature of occult esoteric wisdom in the setting; it has a myth-arc significance that defines all sorcerers. When you say that fire is stolen from the gods, then you're saying that fire is <i>of</i> the gods, whatever else you write about it -- you're saying that it's divine and supernatural and, yes, stolen. Even if it's still 'fire', even if you write other stuff about why the gods had fire and all that, everything about it becomes defined by the basic creation-myth you've attached to it.<br /> <br /> So am I an entitled Solar player? Well, not <i>quite</i>. I think I'm an entitled Sorcerer player. What exactly is wrong with that? I feel that, yes, when I open a book that offers to let me play a sorcerer, and provides the background of the setting's sorcery and all that, that those things should be designed first and foremost around making it fun and exciting and interesting to play a Sorcerer. I feel that if I put down money for a Sorcery book (or for a book that provides a bunch of basic fantasy archetypes, one of which is the sorcerer), that, yeah, I'm entitled to sorcery that feels cool as its own thing.<br /> <br /> Obviously this still has to be balanced around the needs of the rest of the game -- rules for sorcery that are massively better than every other option would feel cool for sorcerers, say, but probably not so much for everyone else. But when it comes to things like the foundational myths of sorcery, those should be written primarily to make Sorcery feel cool, not to make Galactus look cool or to appeal to people who think Galactus is cool. I don't think that's such an unreasonable thing to expect.<br /> <br /> Is this a subjective value-judgment, to an extent? Is this just about the flavor of Sorcery I prefer? Well, sure. If you think that Galactus is awesome and is totally the best thing Marvel ever produced and you want to read more about Galactus everywhere, you're going to be totally happy to read about how Doctor Strange's powers are now derived from the Power Cosmic. But I think it's fair to say that overall, that's a more narrow and limited expression of Sorcery than what the game could offer; going around and rewriting every part of the Marvel universe around Galactus is going to make Galactus fans happy but, probably, you'll end up with a setting that feels smaller, less interesting, and less diverse overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-06-2014, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T02:16:28-07:00","id":106794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to reply to each part individually, because that gets pretty hard to read real fast. But I'll reply to what I think seems to be the gist of your issues with what I said, or at the parts that seem interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... you're going to ignore everything that i've said that blows a hole in your argument... check...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the Sorcerer, as an archetype, is basically about esoteric wisdom -- about someone who sees the occult truth behind the way the world works, and who can manipulate it to their advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything seems good so far...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that the books say about the source through which the Exalted acquired access to sorcery therefore makes a sweeping statement about the nature of occult esoteric wisdom in the setting; it has a myth-arc significance that defines all sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here's where you're wrong. It has just as much impact as you make it have, no more, no less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say that fire is stolen from the gods, then you're saying that fire is <i>of</i> the gods, whatever else you write about it -- you're saying that it's divine and supernatural and, yes, stolen. Even if it's still 'fire', even if you write other stuff about why the gods had fire and all that, everything about it becomes defined by the basic creation-myth you've attached to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stolen, given, does it matter? Your exaltation was made by Sol, empowered by Sol, and given to you by Sol, does that make it less yours? Does that make your deads his? If not, then why this? The Yozi have had far less of an impact on Sorcery (ie. practically none), so why is this a problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So am I an entitled Solar player? Well, not <i>quite</i>. I think I'm an entitled Sorcerer player. What exactly is wrong with that? I feel that, yes, when I open a book that offers to let me play a sorcerer, and provides the background of the setting's sorcery and all that, that those things should be designed first and foremost around making it fun and exciting and interesting to play a Sorcerer. I feel that if I put down money for a Sorcery book (or for a book that provides a bunch of basic fantasy archetypes, one of which is the sorcerer), that, yeah, I'm entitled to sorcery that feels cool as its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is it's own cool thing. They didn't come out and say &quot;All sorcery spells are actually Yozi charms&quot; now did they. Even the Yozi of 2e had initiation charms. That proves once and for all that your argument is full of shit. Now did they have charms that behaved in a sorcery-esque fashion? (Mainly so that they could be dispelled) Yes, but that hardly defines sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously this still has to be balanced around the needs of the rest of the game -- rules for sorcery that are massively better than every other option would feel cool for sorcerers, say, but probably not so much for everyone else. But when it comes to things like the foundational myths of sorcery, those should be written primarily to make Sorcery feel cool, not to make Galactus look cool or to appeal to people who think Galactus is cool. I don't think that's such an unreasonable thing to expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you are being quite unreasonable. The Yozi's learning of Sorcery first, then passing that knowledge on, does nothing to cheapen sorcery, or the sorcerer archetype. On the contrary, I feel that it gives it texture and depth. Sorcery isn't just some nebulous &quot;thing&quot;. Sorcery is the power by which the heavens and earth were created, and fewer things have as much mythic resonance as that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a subjective value-judgment, to an extent?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all this is, and it's based on misremembered facts, exaggerations, and outright lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this just about the flavor of Sorcery I prefer? Well, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>And finally the man is honest!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106786#post106786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think that Galactus is awesome and is totally the best thing Marvel ever produced and you want to read more about Galactus everywhere, you're going to be totally happy to read about how Doctor Strange's powers are now derived from the Power Cosmic. But I think it's fair to say that overall, that's a more narrow and limited expression of Sorcery than what the game could offer; going around and rewriting every part of the Marvel universe around Galactus is going to make Galactus fans happy but, probably, you'll end up with a setting that feels smaller, less interesting, and less diverse overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... maybe gunpowder is too foreign to you, maybe I should use your own example back at you... maybe that will get my point across better... If Galactus discovered higher math (Ie. calculous, trig, and geometry) before humans existed, and maybe even taught it to a favored human, thousands of years ago. Does that in any way diminish modern achievements of engineering, electronics, medicine, or any other field in which we use higher math today? Or is it merely an interesting foot note on the path of our achievements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 04-06-2014, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T03:00:20-07:00","id":106805,"title":"","content":"So... Lunars, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T03:09:06-07:00","id":106807,"title":"","content":"I feel like after 8 pages I can now come back and say that this thread has finally proven to me onr thing: Lunars have no coherent theme behind them.<br /> <br /> It really staggers me that every single example of a Lunar ability that is NOT a form of shapeshifting, is either very generic (and thus indistinguishible from a Solar charm, but with a silver sheen) or is something acomplished through means that aren't specific to Lunars.<br /> <br /> And if that's what Lunars are shaping up to be, a jumbled mess of generic powers, powers ripped off of other Exalted and a limitted ability to shapeshift without any logic behind it, then we're gonna have a one, very disappointing splat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-07-2014, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T03:53:15-07:00","id":106813,"title":"","content":"It's how they were before. But I think the devs will put some thought into it. So far we've only heard a few of their initial ideas. Right now they're concentrating on other things, since the Lunar book won't be out for at least a year, probably two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T04:03:44-07:00","id":106817,"title":"","content":"I'd say that, once we got to the point where some writers had to say &quot;yeah, Brigid learned a Yozi sorcery initiation Charm from Mara, but she refined it later on into a proper Solar one that wouldn't have any traps in it&quot;, one has to acknowledge that the idea is poorly considered and doesn't really fit, since it creates weird roundabout speculations that need additional patches and welds just to keep from collapsing.<br /> <br /> It's about as bad as ideas accumulated by the Yozis and Games of Divinity leading to a point where a writer says &quot;the escaped Yozis won't be able to exterminate humanity, as they would damage the Games of Divinity. For reasons.&quot; The answer is unsatisfying when it hints at the existence of the wrong questions.<br /> <br /> Add in a dash of &quot;it's akin to when they said that Autochthon invented the Sword of Creation&quot;, and one might see why the idea is poorly prioritized.<br /> <br /> (It get's worse when it's used as a basis for a whole &quot;all Primordials have Sorcery&quot; thing, that then runs head on into how Autochthon doesn't really fit with that, so they've got to create an elaborate misdirect saying &quot;he's got initiation, but it's Void-tainted so he can't use it&quot;, which then gets conveniently ignored in an alternate setting where the assumption that Sorcery <i>has</i> to come from Primordials leaves him as the only available source of it, and do you see how this stuff ties itself up in knots trying to maintain credibility?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T04:05:58-07:00","id":106820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106807#post106807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like after 8 pages I can now come back and say that this thread has finally proven to me onr thing: Lunars have no coherent theme behind them. It really staggers me that every single example of a Lunar ability that is NOT a form of shapeshifting, is either very generic (and thus ondistinguishible from a Solar charm, but with a silver sheen) or is something acomplished through means that aren't specific to Lunars. And if that's what Lunars are shaping up to be, a jumbled mess of generic powers, powers ripped off of other Exalted and a limitted ability to shapeshift without any logic behind it, then we're gonna have a one, very disappointing splat...</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's what Lunars are shaping up to be, then I'd say that some manner of legal authority needs to be contacted over how the game has been viciously hijacked from its developers, who are presumably being held captive somewhere to prevent their interference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T04:55:14-07:00","id":106833,"title":"","content":"By all means Isator, show me all those numerous quotes from the developers where they talk about the core theme behind Lunar powers. I'd love to see them. I really really would!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T05:16:04-07:00","id":106843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106753#post106753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The fact that you can take a concept as vast as \u201cThe power and knowledge by which all that is, came to be\u201d and reduce it to \u201clol secrets of the Yozis\u201d tells me much about your position, and mentality. I\u2019m guessing that you\u2019re an self-entitled solar player...</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Can we not resort to this please? Thank you. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T05:25:39-07:00","id":106844,"title":"","content":"Soooooo, what do people here think about Lunar's Territory charms, on one hand, their Patron is a crazy homeless hobo in Yu-Shan, on the other hand, many animal does have the habit of pissing on tree to ward off potential rivals ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T05:32:29-07:00","id":106847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106704#post106704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what will ranged-combat Lunar look like, in Second Edition it's &quot;Use these charms for both closed and ranged attacks&quot; which is pretty boring[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that element of them. It's certainly better than the 1e structure, where they appear to have had distinct Melee and Brawl trees.<br /> <br /> Of course, <i>every</i> Charm shouldn't be cross-compatible, because that would lead to a fairly one-note Charmset, but a smattering of things like Wind-Wings Carry Technique is entirely appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T06:46:32-07:00","id":106864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106844#post106844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooo, what do people here think about Lunar's Territory charms, on one hand, their Patron is a crazy homeless hobo in Yu-Shan, on the other hand, many animal does have the habit of pissing on tree to ward off potential rivals ;D</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the broad concept might need to be adjusted a bit to fit the paradigm of many Lunars not wanting to be tied down to particular places or resources.<br /> <br /> What did they have, a Charm to instantly designate an area as being Owned by them? I feel that one was a bit of an answer to a problem that wasn't already present (I'd assume the regular rules for asserting Ownership should be enough), and a bit of a speed bump for that. I don't think Charms that let you shift your senses around a territory you own are too bad.<br /> <br /> That Charm Sleeping Dragon Awakens... I'm not sure how it would be adjusted, it felt a bit too intricately embedded in the Overdrive concept... maybe something less tied to defending a territory and more to hunting an enemy, might give it a bit more flexibility, give Lunars a bit more incentive to take the fight to others. It might help create an opening for using other Charms; there's still that idea of Charms that require a setup before they can be fired off, other than their mote costs. I wonder if that might be a way to holistically differentiate Lunars from Solars mechanically; their equivalent to Solars having lots of relatively narrow Charms that synergize well in free combos being having some fairly big, powerful Charms that require a fair amount of Lunar flavored setup to use, but it's a setup aided by their narrow Charms.<br /> <br /> Does it still feel like Silver Solars if your ultimate attack, even if it takes the form of a super-powerful punch, requires a lot of stalking and hit-and-run strikes, or for you to have waited and taken a bunch of hits in the fight to pump your blood up or the like? Something that, regardless of its actual vector, you can't fire off until either your opponent is really scared (and bloodied up a bit) or you're really angry (and bloodied up a bit)? Might compensate for it a smidge by having more power than a comparable Solar Charm, but that's not strictly necessary.<br /> <br /> It does put me in mind of that example Holden once came up with while describing a comparison between Essence 5 and 6 Charms.<br /> <br /> When one considers developer and writer comments about approaching Charmsets holistically, about incentivizing distinct playstyles, and puts that against what we know or can infer from the system as it stands, it seems like an easy way to pull away from Silver Solars, or to otherwise differentiate between Exalts with comparable mechanical effects, is to integrate a combination between Charms that need you to act like the Exalt in order to work, and Charms that help you act like the Exalt (or possibly that boost up your setup while you act in that way).<br /> <br /> Ultra Deadly Attack Charm that Requires Stalking + Fairly Good Stalking Charm + Charm that boosts your Return Rate for Stalking = Act more like a Lunar than a Solar?<br /> <br /> Or even, dare I say, Ultra Deadly Attack + Shapeshifting? Where the transformation is not the form of the attack, but part of the vector that lets you build up to it?<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking of the tyrant lizard statblock we were given, which was pretty minimalist, and yet I feel would still give a pretty strong impression of actually fighting a tyrant lizard, where between the need for specific stunts to recharge certain moves and a statement on the conditions under which it will flee, it manages to dodge the sense of just being generic stats tacked on to something that one might worry will fight optimally. It's not much, but it still feels like it'll make tyrant lizards fight like tyrant lizards. Lunars, and Exalted in general, are liable to have considerably more.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, another thing Lunars should be able to do; fight using the capabilities of certain animals without certain particular limitations. Imagine how scary a tyrant lizard that attacks like an intelligent human would be? I'm seeing Titans going around with their hands on the back of their necks here...<br /> <br /> I'm wondering about that being kind of converse as well, now; Intelligence Charms that aid you by reshaping your mind such that you fight more like a beast or devil (represented mechanically by certain modified mental responses, different stunt benefits, what have you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T08:35:28-07:00","id":106915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106712#post106712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Producing <i>multiple limbs/heads</i> doesn't heal any actual health levels, at least not to my knowledge. You still need healing charms for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Losing a limb to an attack is a Crippling effect. It is a lasting form of injury that should not really be readily shucked, even if the limbs were added by HBR. In that case, you'd probably have a &quot;pool&quot; of extremities that needs to heal if damage. That, or make adding extra limbs its own thing, like with Mountainous Spirit Expression and Tyrant Mouse Dominion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:51:15-07:00","id":107092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106805#post106805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Lunars, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha! Now you know how it feels! Behold the sorcerous power of <i>Threefold Binding of the Spotlight!</i><br /> <br /> I'm gonna be honest, I think Lunars are a bit out of place in Exalted, in ways that go beyond just the usual place-in-the-setting stuff we talk about. The core of Exalted draws on two things: Swords-and-sandals fantasy and wuxia action flicks. Those <i>generally</i> do not have a lot of werewolves; while they do have shapeshifters, it's more often presented as something akin to Sorcery than the &quot;core&quot; of your power the way, say, a martial-arts master or a supremely talented swordsman has their thing as the core of their power. Even the Monkey King (and the other characters in Journey to the West), shapeshifting is treated as a sorcerous-style art they study rather than what they are.<br /> <br /> Animal-themed tricksters are a thing, but if you want me to be honest, I don't think they fit well into most of the inspirations Exalted draws on. Having Hercules meet an old master or go up against an empire that wronged him feels appropriate to me; somehow, having him (or any of those other factions) face Anansi feels out of place -- the inspirations Lunars draw on are just a bit disconnected, thematically.<br /> <br /> I think that this is why 1e went for making them &quot;barbarians&quot; and &quot;monsters&quot;. Those are things that fit well into the Swords-and-Sandals world of Exalted. I suspect that that's also why the devs are looking in that direction again despite the risks.<br /> <br /> I think you have to focus on answering that core problem of &quot;how do they fit into the setting?&quot; before you can get the answer to what they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T17:24:24-07:00","id":107163,"title":"","content":"To repeat:<br /> <br /> I think Lunars should also have a <i>visual </i>version of Inevitable Spoor Discovery that detects tracks, even those that no longer exist. Footprints, handprints, fingerprints, faceprints (because sometimes, you get up close and personal with the ground), and tire tracks -- all of these become so apparent to the Lunar's eyes that they might as well glow. While far more limited in discerning the identity of those who interacted with a scene than Inevitable Spoor Discover, &quot;Ghost-Track Kenning&quot; would be infinitely more useful for reconstructing the events that took place at the scene. Which could be represented as a dice-result enhancer for the relevant Investigation action.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T18:57:03-07:00","id":107189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106820#post106820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's what Lunars are shaping up to be, then I'd say that some manner of legal authority needs to be contacted over how the game has been viciously hijacked from its developers, who are presumably being held captive somewhere to prevent their interference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, after seeing some of the Charisma charms from GotMH: Luna, I'd say the primary charm themes of the Lunars, Beastial Prowess, Stewardship, and Loyal Seconds, as well as some others will be covered in a satisfying way, and I have faith that we'll also see a more intuitive framework in the Attribute charm trees this time around.<br /> <br /> Something I hope will be emphasized a little more is the use of Lunar Packs rather than the lone wolf, since as stewards a notable portion of their charms should be geared around cooperating with at least one partner. Just like how some of the Dragon-blooded charms reflected their newly taken station in the world, I'd like to see some traces of second age life in the Lunar charm set and how the formation of packs has influenced their magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T02:13:15-07:00","id":107337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107189#post107189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, after seeing some of the Charisma charms from GotMH: Luna, I'd say the primary charm themes of the Lunars, Beastial Prowess, Stewardship, and Loyal Seconds, as well as some others will be covered in a satisfying way, and I have faith that we'll also see a more intuitive framework in the Attribute charm trees this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm prone to be wary of the Charms in Glories: Luna, since they seem to just exacerbate the problem of a shaky and unfocused theme, but the actual <i>portrayal of Luna</i> still seems to be the single strongest idea space from which one can draw expectations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifnir</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I hope will be emphasized a little more is the use of Lunar Packs rather than the lone wolf, since as stewards a notable portion of their charms should be geared around cooperating with at least one partner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars aren't really stewards anymore. Being guardians of the Realm was a thing that they did, but not what they're for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T02:39:30-07:00","id":107346,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's slow down for a bit here. I know that Lunars should be able to jump really high, punch really hard, be very persuasive or smart and so on and so on, but I want to know <i>why</i> are they able to do those things.<br /> <br /> Like, with Solars I know that they can punch people relly hard, because they're very good at punching people. I know that a Dragon Blooded can jump 20ft high, because he can move like the air. I know a Sidereal can solve difficult mystery case, because he can gain impossible insight from the stars.<br /> <br /> But why is Lunar punching you hard? Why is he able to dodge like the water? Why is he speaking in such a way that you're compelled by his words?<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to say: Lunars punch hard, simply <i>because they're really freakin' strong</i>. They can dodge and dance gracefully, <i>because they're simply really agile</i>. At least, that's what I instinctively imagine being atribute-based Exalts means for Lunars.<br /> <br /> But how do you begin at &quot;being magically strong/agile/resistant/charismatic/manipulative/attractive/smart/cunning/perspective&quot; and arrive at <i>changing into a flock of ravens</i>.<br /> <br /> I just can't draw the connection. I'm left in the dark, nebulous place where I have a good start in the form of baseline atributes and a finish in the form of shapeshifting, but I just can't see the middle. If I can't see the middle, I can hardly come up with examples that are fluid and coherent, not just random ideas out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I wonder if it wouldn't make more sense to leave charms as expressions of atributes and change Lunar shapeshifting into astrology-like gimmick only available to Lunars. At least there would be a clear reasoning behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-07-2014, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T03:43:32-07:00","id":107354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107346#post107346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I wonder if it wouldn't make more sense to leave charms as expressions of atributes and change Lunar shapeshifting into astrology-like gimmick only available to Lunars. At least there would be a clear reasoning behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's how it worked in 2nd ed. You had your attribute charms and your shapeshifting knacks.<br /> But honestly, the difference between dodging because you're really fast, and being good at dodging because you've learned to dodge really well, is pretty small. Essentially just 2m and higher prereqs.<br /> So to avoid the Silver Solar issue, that's why people have been talking about having other ideas behind Lunar charms, such as shapeshifting, being a mythic monster, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T04:45:40-07:00","id":107367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107354#post107354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's how it worked in 2nd ed. You had your attribute charms and your shapeshifting knacks.<br /> But honestly, the difference between dodging because you're really fast, and being good at dodging because you've learned to dodge really well, is pretty small. Essentially just 2m and higher prereqs.<br /> So to avoid the Silver Solar issue, that's why people have been talking about having other ideas behind Lunar charms, such as shapeshifting, being a mythic monster, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;being a mythic monster&quot; is such a meaningless, incoherent, empty phrase that it's either so specific that it can only inspire a couple of ideas cherry-picked from specific sources, or so broad that it can mean whatever you want it to mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-07-2014, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:01:10-07:00","id":107373,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying it's a good theme (I'm not sure it is, for the reasons you say, though it probably has some mileage), I was just saying the reason people* are talking about ideas for monstrous, esoteric, weird physical charms, rather than just &quot;charms for being really strong, charms for being really fast, etc&quot; is because that's what 2nd ed charms were based off of, and there was a lot of Silver Solar stuff (though some charm sets were a lot worse than others, Dex was chock full of it, Appearance was not at all).<br /> 1st ed probably had slightly more esoteric, monstrous stuff... but it was poorly written.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I'd be happy with something equivalent to the Dragon-blood charms, which are ability-based with an elemental theme. So they're not just benders, but they're not just down-powered Solars either.<br /> <br /> *By people, I mean regular posters. The devs haven't said exactly the same as the forumgoers, who seem to be running with this &quot;monsters of myth&quot; idea, but regular posters tend to run away a bit with the small things that devs and writers say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:55:24-07:00","id":107392,"title":"","content":"I'm more concern about how the Obvious keyword manifest in Lunar charms, Infernal/DB/Sidereal have a bunch of different kind of &quot;sparkles&quot; to choose from (red wind, green fire, stone, flower, christmas tree,...) while Lunar can only glow silver, even Abyssal and Solar have more special effect than Lunar, and Solar is the King of Blandness !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T06:01:32-07:00","id":107394,"title":"","content":"If Lunar shapeshifting is anything like Second Edition, and what I've gathered from First Edition, shapeshifting will hardly be a subsystem at all.<br /> <br /> From what I can gather, it was always a case of &quot;you can hunt an animal and drink its blood and then turn into it for a few motes&quot;, with hardly any extra powers or other XP expenditures at all. Everything John has said implies that this will still basically be the case, just with even more utility from what you can turn into; every time you encounter a new animal with some nifty abilities, you can endeavor to be able to turn into it, forever, with no additional cost.<br /> <br /> Maybe it will still have a thing where turning into something huge requires something extra, but tyrant lizards aren't the be all end all of this thing.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting might be present somewhat in their Charms, but I think for the most part, the Lunar capacity to turn into creatures will just be this thing that they have, an additional extrapolation of their transformative nature that is basically off on its own, and also happens to be incredibly useful and versatile, and helps them play differently to others.<br /> <br /> That last word, that's something so many people have honed in on, to little coherence or destination, whether it be &quot;Lunars are versatile because they've got Charms that can be applied to lots of different things&quot; to &quot;Lunars are versatile, so they can get lots and lots of really different Charms&quot; to &quot;Lunars are versatile, so they should switch Charms around like Alchemicals do&quot;. And that last one should be really telling, because Alchemicals are so much more clearly versatile without that seeming to be their <i>thing</i>.<br /> <br /> I feel as though there's been a lot of tripping over in trying to identify Lunars by trying to make Versatility a thing that they are rather than a logical observation about them. Lunars are versatile because, when you approach animals as able to do lots of different useful things, and a person who can really easily acquire an increasing range of things to turn into, well of course they'll be versatile.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'm sure the next question will be &quot;what theme is being expressed by the shapeshifting, and how is it tied into anything else they do&quot;.<br /> <br /> To that I say: I honestly think that there's <i>waaaaaay</i> too much fixation for a while on themes as what Exalts are rather than observations about them. It gets really bad when people examine themes of leadership and responsibility of power in Solars so much that they actually start speculating that Solars should be literally powered by how many followers they have.<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered, Liminals emerged primarily out of a desire to make Frankenstein Exalted. I'm sure that they acquire more details as they went through the vetting process, but the lesson that &quot;more mileage comes out of just deciding what you want given Exalts to be&quot; can probably be widely applied.<br /> <br /> So Lunars are shapeshifters because they want folks who can be shapeshifters. Lunars are a bunch of other things, fierce, mad, relentless, beautiful, devilishly clever, because they want folks like that too (focused in a bit more than with Solars). Characters who display such characteristics essentially tend to have a certain streak labelled as &quot;wild&quot;, so that's a bit of connecting point, but it's not really so big a deal; the combination of everything Lunars have apart from shapeshifting, and the actual shapeshifting, is probably about as syncretic as Solars being the height of arete and literally shining with the power of the Sun.<br /> <br /> It's just the tropes that Exalted constructs for itself, because it's got a very developed setting, but the setting is more than the places and the normals, and that's why, even if Solars are built in emulation of Batman, they still have the additional details that make it seem more worth playing Exalted than playing some licensed DC game. Same goes for whatever Lunars have that may cause literal transformations in their body that are less comprehensive than total shapeshifting. That kind of syncretism is all throughout Exalted, on every level.<br /> <br /> Somebody said that Lunars are a bit out-of-place for shapeshifters in the source material, but I would say that it's more like taking stuff from the source material like the Nemean Lion, the Lernaean Hydra, or that ape creature from that one Conan story, and reinterpreting them as if they were humans, as well as giving them a measure more sophistication; they might be shapeshifters because all those sources are being blended together, but they're mostly that because why not let the Nemean turn into a literal lion (and a few other things) every once in a while, and why limit the sources you're putting together?<br /> <br /> Lunars aren't anthropomorphic animals in their own setting, but they might be a measure of anthropomorphizing animals (or rather, legendary beasts) from other settings, and then starting them off like that.<br /> <br /> (Whereas Fair Folk are those <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/DDxvd\" target=\"_blank\">anthropomorphized Pokemon</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T06:18:05-07:00","id":107397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107394#post107394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunar shapeshifting is anything like Second Edition, and what I've gathered from First Edition, shapeshifting will hardly be a subsystem at all.<br /> <br /> From what I can gather, it was always a case of &quot;you can hunt an animal and drink its blood and then turn into it for a few motes&quot;, with hardly any extra powers or other XP expenditures at all. Everything John has said implies that this will still basically be the case, just with even more utility from what you can turn into; every time you encounter a new animal with some nifty abilities, you can endeavor to be able to turn into it, forever, with no additional cost.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently the entire bestiary is being written with Lunars in mind, giving creatures neat little powers that make you want their shape, I imagine these powers come with the shape at no extra cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T06:29:49-07:00","id":107403,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that a lot of Lunars will have fled into the wilderness following the Usurpation, and as people Exalted throughout the Second Age, not just because it takes the enemy out of their element, but because if you've got the ability to turn into a nifty animal just by stalking and eating it, you're likely to want to spend a fair amount of time out where the animals are.<br /> <br /> I can only imagine how often a Lunar of the First Age might go out on a camping trip or a safari, and come back with a half-dozen new shapes.<br /> <br /> This as something Lunars can do to rapidly accrue power with little personal cultivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T06:52:21-07:00","id":107417,"title":"","content":"Ok, so a theme is descriptive, not prescriptive, like natural laws. Gotcha. But the thing is- it's entirely unhelpful and it shouldn't be the case. Also I don't think it's true.<br /> <br /> See, we have to be able to come up with our own stuff if we want to keep the Lunars (or any other group) interesting. You have to establish <i>some</i> prescriptive terms to make it doable, even if they are really rudementary. With Solars it's human excelence and that's really enough to get us going from straighforward things like punching hard, to really wierd places like growing extra arms in the image of the Uncoquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Lunars aren't physics. If they are to be playable, they can't just be the case for study, we need to deconstruct them, so we know what makes them tick. You really, really can't just treat Lunars as a dumping ground for all the cool ideas inspired by specific sources you want to incorporate into Exalted.<br /> <br /> That is, <i>if</i> they are to be playable. If they are there just to be NPCs, it's fine. But if you want them to be playable and inspiring, they really have to be given some prescriptive qualities, in understandable and objective terms, that inform us exactly what the hell can we do with them.<br /> <br /> Until we're given that, any and all Lunar discussions will always turn into a convulted dumping ground of weird, incoherent ideas, as this thread has shown. Even if those ideas are incredibly cool and we intsinctively want Lunars to have all these cool things, like nightmare-breating, waeather control, territorial charms, transformation charms, <i>they are so incredibly incosistent</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-07-2014, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T07:25:41-07:00","id":107435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107392#post107392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernal/DB/Sidereal have a bunch of different kind of &quot;sparkles&quot; to choose from (red wind, green fire, stone, flower, christmas tree,...)</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my recollection, Sidereals have &quot;glow their one Caste colour&quot;, and that's about it. Maybe they occasionally have slightly fractal patterns or something, but they hardly even have anima banners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">while Lunar can only glow silver</div> </div> </div> </div>And blue, black, purple, white...<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi even has a dark red, I think, and his banner is a kind of rotating wheel of teeth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T07:46:59-07:00","id":107443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107417#post107417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until we're given that, any and all Lunar discussions will always turn into a convulted dumping ground of weird, incoherent ideas, as this thread has shown.</div> </div> </div> </div>What this thread has shown is most likely that hardly anybody in it, myself included, is good at game design, whether they understand what the developers have said or not.<br /> <br /> That and a bunch of people who either don't know or don't care for what the developers have said (including from those people who <i>are</i> good at design, but designing towards entirely different priorities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are to be playable, they can't just be the case for study, we need to deconstruct them, so we know what makes them tick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that if they're to be playable, they just have to have Charms that are useable, including having a decent idea of what they're used for. Homebrew and custom Charms are probably a lot simpler in terms of &quot;don't wildly violate the precedent established by other Charms&quot; rather than &quot;you need to be able to compose the entire Charmset yourself&quot;.<br /> <br /> Second Edition Lunars were weak in regards to what the precedent of other Charms was, but we can probably expect Third Edition to do better. In the meantime, we've got the broad statements from the developers about what Third Edition Lunars shall be, which <i>is</i> consistent; if it's vague, it's vague in the manner that any Exalts would be before you actually saw their Charms. Most people would never extrapolate the Sidereal Charms from a short summary of them, for instance, especially when it's the average rube with no mind for design (even if they might just be able to homebrew a Sidereal Charm or two within the parameters of it).<br /> <br /> Lunars are really pretty unfortunate in that their prior design leaves the fandom with a lot of ideas, but not much actual shape, whereas people more-or-less know what to expect of Sidereals, so the most contentious thing there tends to be either the closed Charmset issue, or a couple of surrounding incidentals, this despite the fact that I can bet you that a summary of Sidereals like what we've had for Lunars would be even <i>less</i> readily grasped.<br /> <br /> But none of us are being asked to design the Lunars, so it doesn't really matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T07:55:48-07:00","id":107447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107435#post107435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And blue, black, purple, white...<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi even has a dark red, I think, and his banner is a kind of rotating wheel of teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was talking more about Charms than Anima's color though. Claw of the SILVER Moon, Purging the Tarnished SILVER, Invulnerable MoonSILVER Caparace,....etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T08:21:09-07:00","id":107457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106844#post106844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooo, what do people here think about Lunar's Territory charms, on one hand, their Patron is a crazy homeless hobo in Yu-Shan, on the other hand, many animal does have the habit of pissing on tree to ward off potential rivals ;D</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, a Charm that lets you piss on a rock or scratch up a tree to ward people off doesn't sound like a half-bad idea. That is, as just one application of a way to create wards that inspire Fear in anyone who sees them; a Fear that persists if they dare to cross the marker, and only goes away a while after they have fled from it. (This Charm would be related to Scar-Making Blow, which imparts scars charged with visible emotion and meaning.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T08:23:42-07:00","id":107459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106701#post106701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm upset that <i>2e retconned the Yozi into inventing Sorcery</i>. There's an extremely huge difference.<br /> <br /> (Again, it's the difference between saying &quot;I'm annoyed that this writer retconned Doctor Strange into having his powers derived from Galactus&quot; and &quot;I'm annoyed that the Silver Surfer uses the power of Galactus.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not a retcon.<br /> <br /> The legendary account about the origins of sorcery way back in in the Book of Three Circles (the first edition magic supplement published in September 2001) has Brigid approached by a &quot;forest-spirit&quot; whose description matches the second-circle demon Mara (from the first edition Storyteller's Companion), and the whole situation pretty much matches the summoning parameters for Mara (someone crying over their lost/separated love, shedding tears into a spring, in the forest; a shooting star appears, which is also a sign that Mara is coming). The whole thing fits together all too well to be accidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T08:34:03-07:00","id":107460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107457#post107457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, a Charm that lets you piss on a rock or scratch up a tree to ward people off doesn't sound like a half-bad idea. That is, as just one application of a way to create wards that inspire Fear in anyone who sees them; a Fear that persists if they dare to cross the marker, and only goes away a while after they have fled from it. (This Charm would be related to Scar-Making Blow, which imparts scars charged with visible emotion and meaning.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That post was an insult again Lunar's animal-ness, but your post does make the hypothetical &quot;piss on tree&quot; charm sound so awesome, I do love dark forest with scary scratch-marks make by some<i>thing</i>, creepy rock-piles or dolls with their inside rip-out scatters everywhere. A Blair Witch Lunar is so much better than a stereotype werewolf Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:13:29-07:00","id":107484,"title":"","content":"A Lunar Blair Witch wouldn't have taken like three days to finally kill the teens, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:13:44-07:00","id":107485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107460#post107460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That post was an insult again Lunar's animal-ness, but your post does make the hypothetical &quot;piss on tree&quot; charm sound so awesome, I do love dark forest with scary scratch-marks make by some<i>thing</i>, creepy rock-piles or dolls with their inside rip-out scatters everywhere. A Blair Witch Lunar is so much better than a stereotype werewolf Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div> (It goes to show that any inspiration can be mocked, or made awesome.) Also, you can mix things up with a Charm that does the opposite; rather than a Fear Ward, a Desire Bait, which tempts people to come closer to a thing, whether it be a blood trail the wounded Lunar deliberately left behind, or a woman's clothes trailing to her bedroom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-07-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:25:54-07:00","id":107488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107459#post107459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a retcon.<br /> <br /> The legendary account about the origins of sorcery way back in in the Book of Three Circles (the first edition magic supplement published in September 2001) has Brigid approached by a &quot;forest-spirit&quot; whose description matches the second-circle demon Mara (from the first edition Storyteller's Companion), and the whole situation pretty much matches the summoning parameters for Mara (someone crying over their lost/separated love, shedding tears into a spring, in the forest; a shooting star appears, which is also a sign that Mara is coming). The whole thing fits together all too well to be accidental.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, this was an easter egg in 1e, but it was definitely there. Note that <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaranephilpal/OriginsOfSorcery\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> predates the second edition somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:28:36-07:00","id":107489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107459#post107459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a retcon.<br /> <br /> The legendary account about the origins of sorcery way back in in the Book of Three Circles (the first edition magic supplement published in September 2001) has Brigid approached by a &quot;forest-spirit&quot; whose description matches the second-circle demon Mara (from the first edition Storyteller's Companion), and the whole situation pretty much matches the summoning parameters for Mara (someone crying over their lost/separated love, shedding tears into a spring, in the forest; a shooting star appears, which is also a sign that Mara is coming). The whole thing fits together all too well to be accidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was Mara concieved <i>before</i> or <i>after</i> that description? Because that does sound like a self-fulfilling prophecy if I ever heard one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-07-2014, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:36:43-07:00","id":107495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107346#post107346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, let's slow down for a bit here. I know that Lunars should be able to jump really high, punch really hard, be very persuasive or smart and so on and so on, but I want to know <i>why</i> are they able to do those things.<br /> <br /> Like, with Solars I know that they can punch people relly hard, because they're very good at punching people. I know that a Dragon Blooded can jump 20ft high, because he can move like the air. I know a Sidereal can solve difficult mystery case, because he can gain impossible insight from the stars.<br /> <br /> But why is Lunar punching you hard? Why is he able to dodge like the water? Why is he speaking in such a way that you're compelled by his words?<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to say: Lunars punch hard, simply <i>because they're really freakin' strong</i>. They can dodge and dance gracefully, <i>because they're simply really agile</i>. At least, that's what I instinctively imagine being atribute-based Exalts means for Lunars.<br /> <br /> But how do you begin at &quot;being magically strong/agile/resistant/charismatic/manipulative/attractive/smart/cunning/perspective&quot; and arrive at <i>changing into a flock of ravens</i>.<br /> <br /> I just can't draw the connection. I'm left in the dark, nebulous place where I have a good start in the form of baseline atributes and a finish in the form of shapeshifting, but I just can't see the middle. If I can't see the middle, I can hardly come up with examples that are fluid and coherent, not just random ideas out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I wonder if it wouldn't make more sense to leave charms as expressions of atributes and change Lunar shapeshifting into astrology-like gimmick only available to Lunars. At least there would be a clear reasoning behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it needs to be seen as so incoherent. A lot of (maybe most?) Lunar Attribute charms are actually shapeshifting effects, including most of the combat charms. Hide-Toughening Essence, Armor-Forming Technique, Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace are soak charms, and all involve shapeshifting. The healing charms seem either explicitly shapeshifting or could be explained as shapeshifting. Claws of the Silver Moon is definitely shapeshifting. Perception charms like Eyes of the Cat can also be explained as shapeshifting if you want to.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar punches really hard or jumps really high, why can't you just assume it's because he's shaped her muscles into steel? That's always been my assumption. The general theme is that Lunars adapt themselves; whatever they do, they do through change and adaptation.<br /> <br /> Of course, being Exalted by the power of a Celestial Incarna does give you certain divine power all by itself, regardless of whatever shapeshifting powers you might also acquire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107392#post107392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more concern about how the Obvious keyword manifest in Lunar charms, Infernal/DB/Sidereal have a bunch of different kind of &quot;sparkles&quot; to choose from (red wind, green fire, stone, flower, christmas tree,...) while Lunar can only glow silver, even Abyssal and Solar have more special effect than Lunar, and Solar is the King of Blandness !</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno what you mean exactly, but there's room for a lot of personalization in terms of special effects. Demonstrative bragging technique: the only character I'm currently playing has an anima banner materializing as <i>white petals surrounding a stylized coyote amid shifting patterns of light and darkness. </i>The petals are of night-blossoming rain lily (Cooperia pedunculata), and materialize whenever his anima is at the 8+ level or he uses any Charm with the Obvious keyword. His Tell is their lingering scent, always present but rarely noticed.<br /> <br /> The latter fluff is because my ST has permitted me to use the Past Life Background normally limited to Infernals, representing the character's inheritance of the soul and the exaltation of a powerful elder. When the Background effect kicks in, the coyote disappears entirely and is replaced by a burning white rain lily in the air, the penumbra of light and shadow becomes a steady canescent blaze, he changes from male to female and his caste goes from No Moon to Full Moon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107447#post107447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I was talking more about Charms than Anima's color though. Claw of the SILVER Moon, Purging the Tarnished SILVER, Invulnerable MoonSILVER Caparace,....etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, silver is a nice color. It's well suited for stuff happening at night - which is another theme of Lunars that we don't hear much about. And it looks nice if the game is happening in your head as a black and white comic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-07-2014, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:39:57-07:00","id":107498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107489#post107489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Mara concieved <i>before</i> or <i>after</i> that description? Because that does sound like a self-fulfilling prophecy if I ever heard one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mara was published in the ST Companion in August 2001, a month before BoTC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:48:59-07:00","id":107502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107495#post107495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it needs to be seen as so incoherent. A lot of (maybe most?) Lunar Attribute charms are actually shapeshifting effects, including most of the combat charms. Hide-Toughening Essence, Armor-Forming Technique, Invulnerable Moonsilver Carapace are soak charms, and all involve shapeshifting. The healing charms seem either explicitly shapeshifting or could be explained as shapeshifting. Claws of the Silver Moon is definitely shapeshifting. Perception charms like Eyes of the Cat can also be explained as shapeshifting if you want to.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar punches really hard or jumps really high, why can't you just assume it's because he's shaped her muscles into steel? That's always been my assumption. The general theme is that Lunars adapt themselves; whatever they do, they do through change and adaptation.<br /> <br /> Of course, being Exalted by the power of a Celestial Incarna does give you certain divine power all by itself, regardless of whatever shapeshifting powers you might also acquire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assume this and would gladly do. Or anything else that makes as much sense and is coherent and inspiring enough to think of charms. But that particular train of thought has some implications and if you're willing to follow that strain of thought into it's logical conclusion, you arrive at Infernals.<br /> <br /> I think devs said that Lunars aren't specifically shapeshifters and shapeshifting is just an addition to the things they do. But it's frustrating, because they never clarified <i>what is the principle behind Lunars doing their basic stuff</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not about what I assume for now, about Lunars as they are, it's about what is the principle for 3e Lunars. There should be one. Or at least several, if we just have to have messy Lunars. But please, let it be there and clear instead of being inferred from studying Lunars. Seriously, I thought they wanted to make this edition more streamlined, <i>if I have to study Lunars to achieve basic understanding of their themes, they failed</i>. It's just that easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-07-2014, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:56:36-07:00","id":107505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107502#post107502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you're willing to follow that train of thought into it's logical conclusion, you arrive at Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107502#post107502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think devs said that Lunars aren't specifically shapeshifters and shapeshifting is just an addition to the things they do. But it's frustrating, because they never clarified what is the principle behind Lunars doing their basic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, Luna is still going to be an ever-changing god/dess of infinite forms, never looking the same from one appearance to the next, the celestial embodiment of change... so although Lunars aren't <u>just</u> shapeshifters, I fully expect that shapeshifting is going to be seen as the most basic and central thing they are. Morke has said that the connection to animals comes from Luna's connection to Gaia; from that, I interpret that it's not something actually inherent to Lunars, just something they all have because of the connection to Luna to Gaia. In other words, they embody shapeshifting more than they embody beasts. That was the case in 2nd Edition also.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107502#post107502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about what I assume for now, about Lunars as they are, it's about what is the principle for 3e Lunars. There should be one. Or at least several, if we just have to have messy Lunars. But please, let it be there and clear instead of being inferred from studying Lunars. Seriously, I thought they wanted to make this edition more streamlined, <i>if I have to study Lunars to achieve basic understanding of their themes, they failed</i>. It's just that easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're right, of course. I can't help pointing out, though, that the clearer the devs are about what Lunars are, the more forumites are guaranteed to say their definition is too narrow and restrictive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T10:02:48-07:00","id":107512,"title":"","content":"Well, I can only say I hope you're right and that I expect you to be wrong!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T10:04:11-07:00","id":107513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107484#post107484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lunar Blair Witch wouldn't have taken like three days to finally kill the teens, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree a Lunar Blair Witch would certainly have been capable of killing them quicker. Whether she necessarily would might depend on her motives, what else is happening, and the specifics of those powers.<br /> <br /> &quot;They're just stupid teenagers,&quot; the Lunar could reasonably and correctly think. &quot;I have more important things to do than slaughter them myself. I'll just keep an eye on them as they go stupidly marching through my terror wards. <i>If</i> they continue not to give it up for another day or two, <i>then</i> I will take time out to pay them the wages of stupidity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T13:57:01-07:00","id":107664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107092#post107092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having Hercules meet an old master or go up against an empire that wronged him feels appropriate to me; somehow, having him (or any of those other factions) face Anansi feels out of place -- the inspirations Lunars draw on are just a bit disconnected, thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, Herakles specifically <i>did </i>fight and kill a shapeshifting demigod (quasigod? Poseidon was his grandfather) named Periklymenos. In the course of the fight, Periklymenos assumed five different forms: Ant, lion, snake, eagle, and swarm of bees. (Since he could become a <i>swarm </i>of bees, I presume the form of a single ant was intended for an ambush.)<br /> <br /> Yeah, I didn't know about <a href=\"http://www.theoi.com/Heros/Periklymenos.html\" target=\"_blank\">the shapeshifting Prince of Pylos</a> either, until I read Riordan's <i>Son of Poseidon.</i> Ironically, he's not very well-known anymore, for a guy whose name meant &quot;All-Around Famous&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you have to focus on answering that core problem of &quot;how do they fit into the setting?&quot; before you can get the answer to what they can do. </div> </div> </div>I think they're supposed to be that splat who, even when they're allies to the Solars, Sidereals and Terrestrials, those hosts have good reasons to wonder if the Lunars are monsters. I mean, they kill people and eat their hearts, man.<br /> <br /> It was really easy for the Immaculate Order to paint the Lunar Exalted as Anathema, and the Lunar Exalted very easily justified them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-07-2014, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T14:53:18-07:00","id":107720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107664#post107664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're supposed to be that splat who, even when they're allies to the Solars, Sidereals and Terrestrials, those hosts have good reasons to wonder if the Lunars are monsters. I mean, they kill people and eat their hearts, man.<br /> <br /> It was really easy for the Immaculate Order to paint the Lunar Exalted as Anathema, and the Lunar Exalted very easily justified them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flip-side of the classic World of Darkness, where werewolves are definitely monsters but can strive to be more, even if not everyone necessarily acknowledges that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T15:31:26-07:00","id":107739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107459#post107459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a retcon.<br /> <br /> The legendary account about the origins of sorcery way back in in the Book of Three Circles (the first edition magic supplement published in September 2001) has Brigid approached by a &quot;forest-spirit&quot; whose description matches the second-circle demon Mara (from the first edition Storyteller's Companion), and the whole situation pretty much matches the summoning parameters for Mara (someone crying over their lost/separated love, shedding tears into a spring, in the forest; a shooting star appears, which is also a sign that Mara is coming). The whole thing fits together all too well to be accidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it implies that Mara is one of the many diverse spirits <i>involved</i> in Brigid's journey to enlightenment. Demons are part of the rich tapestry of Creation's magic.<br /> <br /> But she isn't the entire story, and nothing in there implies that she's any more meaningful to the overarching story of Sorcery than anyone else Brigid met in her journey. Neph fixated on her appearance in the story and ignored the fact that Brigid had to make contact with <i>every other aspect of Creation's magic</i> as well. (Again, part of the story involves an extended stay with a lord of the Fair Folk, which makes no sense if you go by 2e's version.) The way I read it is always &quot;Brigid's story had to touch on all of the aspects of creation's magic, which includes demons; but we will be subtle about demons because they have heavier implications than the others and not everyone will want to recognize that they have an important role in Creation's supernatural landscape.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2e retconned that to &quot;the story of Brigid is about how she was handed the secrets of Sorcery by Mara and the rest of her journey was not important&quot;, which is not <i>at all</i> what was present in the original. Mara's (implied) visit with Brigid is one chapter in a larger narrative of how she attained enlightenment; but the 1e story is not at all focused on Mara or the Primordials the way 2e retconned it.<br /> <br /> 1e's version is a subtle (allegorical) story about a journey to enlightenment which makes the statement that Sorcery is broad and mysterious and transcends any one aspect of the universe to encompass the underlying truth of the whole; 2e's version is, basically, that the <i>Yozis</i> are broad and mysterious and transcendent and therefore gave this Sorcery thing to the Exalted for their own reasons. One is a story about how awesome sorcery is, and the other is a story about how awesome the Yozis are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-07-2014, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T15:47:45-07:00","id":107743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107720#post107720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flip-side of the classic World of Darkness, where werewolves are definitely monsters but can strive to be more, even if not everyone necessarily acknowledges that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is reminding me of some thoughts I posted over at Space Battles:<br /> <br /> <br /> The story of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loathly_lady\" target=\"_blank\">Loathly Lady</a> seems like an excellent vehicle for communicating the &quot;Beauty and Ugliness&quot; that I see as a characteristic of Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted are the purest beauty, always beautiful. Abyssals are hideous; they can play at beauty, but it's a disturbing beauty that doesn't truly hide what's wrong with them. Infernals are terrible in their beauty.<br /> <br /> I think Lunars are the ones capable of being tremendously ugly yet also wholesomely beautiful. Not the tainted beauty of the Infernals, the fake beauty of the Abyssals, or the constant beauty of the Solar Exalted. When the Lunars are beautiful, they are as lovely as the Solars, but when they get ugly, they get as ugly as the worst.<br /> <br /> The lady and the monster. The ugly witch, the beautiful beast. The light and dark sides of the moon.<br /> <br /> The story of the Loathly Lady also provides a plot through which to tie that duality with the concept of the Solar Mate, or the more general idea of the one person or people around whom a Lunar centers her identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T16:05:40-07:00","id":107754,"title":"","content":"Can we put Aquillion, like, on the dev team or something? He speaks the words of wisdom. We need more of that wisdom. It's a good wisdom.<br /> <br /> It's a rather out-of-place wisdom in this thread, but wisdom is wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T16:37:39-07:00","id":107772,"title":"","content":"Not so much a request as a question, but do you think you can use Mockingbird Persona Mimicry (from Shards) to alter the identity conveyed by the 4 mote version of Foe-Marking Style (post-Errata)?*<br /> <br /> Also, is there anyone who believes that Mockingbird Persona Mimicry shouldn't work for anything the Lunar creates, rather than just text messages? Pictures, sculptures or even swords, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> * For those who don't remember, you can spend four motes when scarring someone so that anyone who sees the scar instantly knows it was you who did it, how you feel about the scarred individual (beloved son or hated enemy) and that you are not someone to be crossed (such as by harming the son or helping the enemy).<br /> <br /> This function of the Charm doesn't actually compel any action or inaction in a mechanical sense, though upgrades could certainly change that. Perhaps upgrades which allow you to turn the person himself into a Fearful Ward or Desirable Bait?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-07-2014, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T17:23:00-07:00","id":107792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107739#post107739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e's version is a subtle (allegorical) story about a journey to enlightenment which makes the statement that Sorcery is broad and mysterious and transcends any one aspect of the universe to encompass the underlying truth of the whole; 2e's version is, basically, that the <i>Yozis</i> are broad and mysterious and transcendent and therefore gave this Sorcery thing to the Exalted for their own reasons. One is a story about how awesome sorcery is, and the other is a story about how awesome the Yozis are.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e certainly did not handle it particularly well, but there were a <i>hell</i> of a lot of players in 1e who took on the &quot;demons intentionally led the Exalted to discover sorcery&quot; aspect of it. This is not particularly surprising, since it's an appealing notion on multiple levels! While I'm sure it occasionally happened, at no point did I see it taken to be &quot;a story about how awesome the Yozis are&quot;. My experience was that the Yozis were almost completely absent from 1e games except by allusion, and people went to fetich souls when they wanted demonic big bads.<br /> <br /> My experience is, I'm sure, different from many people's. But trying to tear up something we had a good, productive time with in two thousand god damned three because of how shit got fucked up far later for unrelated reasons, after most of us had stopped paying attention to 2e because 2e was bad, is annoying to me. We also liked and did fine with the presentation of the Yozis in GoD, for what it's worth.<br /> <br /> I am not very sympathetic to attempts to project the sins of late 2e, seen in hindsight, to a time so far back in the mists of history that people still thought the Matrix sequels might be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-07-2014, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T18:16:21-07:00","id":107826,"title":"","content":"Do y'all think there's enough mileage in the concept of a Charm that lets you intimidate someone without being penalized by your appearance (such as being mortally wounded or in the form of a cute little bunny) and a Charm that lets you seduce someone without being penalized (such as for being caked with mud, or gnarled with age)?<br /> <br /> Would those options be any more interesting than an &quot;Intimidate&quot; or &quot;Seduce&quot; simple-type Charm which worked regardless of what you looked like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T19:11:48-07:00","id":107876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107826#post107826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do y'all think there's enough mileage in the concept of a Charm that lets you intimidate someone without being penalized by your appearance (such as being mortally wounded or in the form of a cute little bunny) and a Charm that lets you seduce someone without being penalized (such as for being caked with mud, or gnarled with age)?<br /> <br /> Would those options be any more interesting than an &quot;Intimidate&quot; or &quot;Seduce&quot; simple-type Charm which worked regardless of what you looked like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the impression I got was that the Solar Charm set's &quot;helix&quot; structures wouldn't be standard, but it definitely sounded like the EX3 team has an eye for synergies. I could see takes on both Charms working fitting in and working together.<br /> <br /> I would personally find the 'without being penalized' sorts of Charms more interesting. But I also admit I'm overfond of Lunars turning into animals that are clearly unsuited to a task and then nevertheless succeeding with panache. That said, I could see a case against that kind of thing: if Lunars tend to excel at a task by changing themselves in ways such that they will excel at it, their magic may not give much support for excelling with changes that would be actively bad for the task.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, even if true, perhaps succeeding -- or merely attempting -- despite such a handicap might have its own benefits. I don't know what, but some sort of perk for giving people strong emotional reactions where never in a million years would they have expected to find them. It's one thing to be frightened of a tiger or attracted to a nubile youth. It's a very different one if such fear and attraction are respectively inspired by a li'l baby bunny and a nonagenarian covered with filth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 04-07-2014, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T20:00:22-07:00","id":107912,"title":"","content":"Outside of outright transformation, I feel a lunar should remind those who look upon them of animals and mythic monsters with every move they make. Someone mentioned earlier that a lunar jumping on one from above should look like a flock of ravens descending upon you. Things like that: cunning as a wolf, slippery like a snake, climbs like a squirrel, leaps like a cat, roars like a dragon... okay maybe not EVERY move, but it should still be a strong theme with them. Ya know?<br /> <br /> On Solar versus Lunar: XP, BP and other such things equal, a lunar should be strong enough to beat a Solar in an area that the Solar hasn't specialized. What I know of Lunar fluff suggests that Lunars are more versatile, but Solars are stronger in their specific skillsets.<br /> <br /> Sorcerey: I've heard it said Lunars should be the masters of Sorcerey... whiiiich is a little odd imho considering that, as I just finished saying, a specialized Solar is usually gonna be better at whatever they throw themselves into, but it could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T20:05:38-07:00","id":107914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107876#post107876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, even if true, perhaps succeeding -- or merely attempting -- despite such a handicap might have its own benefits. I don't know what, but some sort of perk for giving people strong emotional reactions where never in a million years would they have expected to find them. It's one thing to be frightened of a tiger or attracted to a nubile youth. It's a very different one if such fear and attraction are respectively inspired by a li'l baby bunny and a nonagenarian covered with filth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more about the shock and confusion of spectators when the victim is inexplicably frightened by a small, cute child.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dude, what is your problem? He's just a kid!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's the devil in disguise!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Right, I think you've had enough to drink.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Along similar lines, I can imagine a Lunar Charm which causes people without any Intimacy towards you to be treated as if they had a minor one appropriate to the way you're behaving. So as long as you treat people warmly and politely, they can be treated as if they had a minor Intimacy of friendship with you.<br /> <br /> It has no effect on people who already have an Intimacy for you, but if someone who hates you is in the party where you are behaving cordially, everyone else is going to react as though that person is being hostile to their friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-07-2014, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T22:29:43-07:00","id":107984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=107484#post107484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lunar Blair Witch wouldn't have taken like three days to finally kill the teens, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well she needed to study them so she could properly take their heart's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T09:24:17-07:00","id":108253,"title":"","content":"I always kind of wanted a Lunar charm that caused specific people of your choice to realize that you were a shapeshifting monster in disguise, so you could gaslight them. Might be too specific, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:55:45-07:00","id":108484,"title":"","content":"I still very much want a Perception Charm that tells you who and what a specific person thinks you are. Very handy for knowing when your cover's blown, or for when even YOU don't know exactly whose face you're wearing. Or at least what their relationship was with the person you're dealing with right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:58:38-07:00","id":108487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108484#post108484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still very much want a Perception Charm that tells you who and what a specific person thinks you are. Very handy for knowing when your cover's blown, or for when even YOU don't know exactly whose face you're wearing. Or at least what their relationship was with the person you're dealing with right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd Edition, could you use Motive-Dissecting Eye for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T13:22:48-07:00","id":108505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108487#post108487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 2nd Edition, could you use Motive-Dissecting Eye for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. It doesn't let you read thoughts as such. Just the intent to take part in an action, desire for something, or an emotional state. You could tell that someone was suspicious, but the Charm wouldn't be able to parse suspicion from full knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:21:53-07:00","id":108741,"title":"","content":"I'm a TAW fan. I get the impression that's a bit of a pariah these days, or that mentioning it when talking about 3e Lunars is a faux pas but here goes. I mentioned a whiiile back, on the last forum I think, that I think 3e Lunars is going to be a lot like TAW Lunars, thematically, they'll just be using different words for it (&quot;scary monster&quot; vs &quot;terrifying witches&quot;). TAW's words and theming seemed to make it favor No and Changing Moons, because that's what you get with witches, and 3e's mention of monsters favors Full moons. TAW delivered on making its Full Moons interesting and the developers promise to deliver on making Changing and No Moons interesting.<br /> <br /> That was my hitch with 2e Lunars, it favored Full Moons (And T-Rexes). I read one Exalted campaign, back on OotS's forum, and it was all Solars except for one guy, a Lunar. He was a Full Moon (And a T-Rex). I read KoC, and Marena gives me the impression she would have so many less problems if she were a Full Moon (And a T-Rex).<br /> <br /> So, TAW. It's cardinal sin, perhaps, was being 2e. And having some rabid fans. And also trying not to step on too many toes when it came to rewriting Creation's history to include them. It gave me a reason to play a Lunar and not be a Full Moon (Or a T-Rex).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:36:39-07:00","id":108757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108741#post108741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, TAW. It's cardinal sin, perhaps, was being 2e. And having some rabid fans. And also trying not to step on too many toes when it came to rewriting Creation's history to include them. It gave me a reason to play a Lunar and not be a Full Moon (Or a T-Rex).</div> </div> </div> </div>TAW's cardinal sin was its fans trumpeting it as a great replacement for canon lunars while some how being oblivious to the fact they are silver Infernals. Nothing wrong with silver infernals mind you (as a fun fan splat) but at some point it moved from fun fan work to &quot;one true vision for all Lunars now and future&quot;. Which is a problem with the whole reskinned Infernals thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:41:19-07:00","id":108761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108757#post108757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TAW's cardinal sin was its fans trumpeting it as a great replacement for canon lunars while some how being oblivious to the fact they are silver Infernals. Nothing wrong with silver infernals mind you (as a fun fan splat) but at some point it moved from fun fan work to &quot;one true vision for all Lunars now and future&quot;. Which is a problem with the whole reskinned Infernals thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>TAW outright stole some Infernal charms, took the Sidereal's approach to its individual trees and largely stole the Abyssal's theme of 'entropy' and 'terror'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:47:28-07:00","id":108767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108505#post108505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. It doesn't let you read thoughts as such. Just the intent to take part in an action, desire for something, or an emotional state. You could tell that someone was suspicious, but the Charm wouldn't be able to parse suspicion from full knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can tell you the target's motivaiton, her primary virtue, her intimacies, emotional state, or any &quot;current intention, desire or emotion, including intent to attack someone.&quot; I don't know, I think the last part might accomodate desires like, <i>desire to unmask my target,</i> <i>desire to alert the guards, desire to fool silver anathema into thinking I haven't caught on, desire to get away from said anathema in one piece...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-08-2014, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:56:04-07:00","id":108775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108767#post108767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can tell you the target's motivaiton, her primary virtue, her intimacies, emotional state, or any &quot;current intention, desire or emotion, including intent to attack someone.&quot; I don't know, I think somewhere in and between those things, it could probably let you know if your cover's been blown or not. &quot;Desire to unmask me,&quot; &quot;desire to alert the guards,&quot; &quot;desire to get away from silver anathema in one piece,&quot; etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it wouldn't tell you who or what that person thought you were.<br /> <br /> I kill and eat a dude who attacked me in the middle of the night. I use his face to infiltrate a town, and then this woman appears and starts shouting at me like I kicked her dog.<br /> <br /> I use Silver Mirror Insight to determine if she thinks I'm her friend, husband or brother, which allows me to respond more appropriately without blowing my cover. A brother addressing her like a husband would throw up flags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T17:02:18-07:00","id":108778,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see. You're right, it wouldn't do that. I guess I misread your comment.<br /> <br /> Well, it doesn't do what you want exactly, but in that situation at least, Blood-Kin Sense?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;By spending four motes instead, the Lunar may simply declare an individual (whom the character must have met). Then, the Charm serves to determine the target\u2019s relationship with the named individual and the importance thereof to the target.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:16:00-07:00","id":108828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108778#post108778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I see. You're right, it wouldn't do that. I guess I misread your comment.<br /> <br /> Well, it doesn't do what you want exactly, but in that situation at least, Blood-Kin Sense?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;By spending four motes instead, the Lunar may simply declare an individual (whom the character must have met). Then, the Charm serves to determine the target\u2019s relationship with the named individual and the importance thereof to the target.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I'd forgotten about Blood-Kin Sense because of how bad it was, in design, and placement, and comparison to a Dragon-Blooded Charm.<br /> <br /> I agree that Blood-Kin Sense, or a version of it, could cover the basic idea I'm going for.<br /> <br /> It and Motive-Dissecting Eye still don't quite cover all of the applications I'm looking for, but it's arguable if that's a flaw or a feature. Also, upgrades are a possibility.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:35:34-07:00","id":108835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=106864#post106864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did they have, a Charm to instantly designate an area as being Owned by them? I feel that one was a bit of an answer to a problem that wasn't already present (I'd assume the regular rules for asserting Ownership should be enough), and a bit of a speed bump for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There weren't particularly rules for asserting Ownership over anything; the Corebook had a rule of thumb which worked for objects and vehicles, but landscapes exist literally on a different scale.<br /> <br /> As a way to claim ownership over an entire populated village without being the chief or even one of the people living there, Boundary-Marking Meditation was <i>not </i>merely a speed-bump. In less than an hour (or the time that it would take to race around the village in the form of a wolf), you could transform the village into a place your territory-reliant Charms would work, which would help in turning the place into a defensible death-trap for invaders.<br /> <br /> Let's also not forget the -1 external penalty imposes on unwelcome intruders with absolutely no action or mote-commitment on your part. It's not even keyworded. Between that and the fact that native gods &quot;accept the Lunar's primacy&quot; (roleplaying and stunting opportunities when dealing with them!), this isn't simply a Charm which is only good for enabling other Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think Charms that let you shift your senses around a territory you own are too bad. </div> </div> </div>They're better if the Charm works even when you're not in the territory anymore, even if all it tells you is whether or not someone crossed your borders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That Charm Sleeping Dragon Awakens... I'm not sure how it would be adjusted, it felt a bit too intricately embedded in the Overdrive concept... </div> </div> </div>Easy; exchange the Overdrive mechanic with the Momentum/Advantage mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T23:16:07-07:00","id":109018,"title":"","content":"I liked Lunar Territory charms. <br /> <br /> I'd love to see that return, especially if we got charms that allowed a Lunar to summon forth aspects of his Territory onto the current landscape. Perhaps summon up a grove of trees, or a castle, or a lake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T02:23:44-07:00","id":109117,"title":"","content":"I think a really good example of a non-shapeshifting Lunar would be Copperhead from the Arkham Origins video game. Everything about her screams venomous snake. Her movements, body language, that she specializes in grappling and flexibility and her weapon is a claw that dispenses poison. All of it infers a snake-like totem, but not once does she shapeshift into a snake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T19:18:30-07:00","id":110496,"title":"","content":"So I finally found the copy I made of the spoiler for 3rdEd's Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe, and I tried to convert it into a Lunar Charm.<br /> <br /> Didn't feel right at all. Almost immediately I stopped and asked myself, &quot;Why is the Lunar targeting the leader and producing a trickle-down effect? Wouldn't it make more sense for the Lunar Charm to target and affect individuals regardless of their social status?&quot;<br /> <br /> I figure the Lunar can use such a Charm against a leader who trusts or loves her, as the Solar must do with the Socialize Charm, but it wouldn't create a Defining-level Principle in the leader with such an instant and wide-spread societal impact. Perhaps the Lunar could create a Major Intimacy of fear or lust towards particular things, and it's left to the leader to interpret his policies around that emotion and to convince his people to follow his lead if it strikes them as unwise on the face of it.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted get to exploit social structures with Socialize and Bureaucracy Charms in a way that Lunars just shouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T21:33:30-07:00","id":110585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110496#post110496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I finally found the copy I made of the spoiler for 3rdEd's Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe, and I tried to convert it into a Lunar Charm.<br /> <br /> Didn't feel right at all. Almost immediately I stopped and asked myself, &quot;Why is the Lunar targeting the leader and producing a trickle-down effect? Wouldn't it make more sense for the Lunar Charm to target and affect individuals regardless of their social status?&quot;<br /> <br /> I figure the Lunar can use such a Charm against a leader who trusts or loves her, as the Solar must do with the Socialize Charm, but it wouldn't create a Defining-level Principle in the leader with such an instant and wide-spread societal impact. Perhaps the Lunar could create a Major Intimacy of fear or lust towards particular things, and it's left to the leader to interpret his policies around that emotion and to convince his people to follow his lead if it strikes them as unwise on the face of it.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted get to exploit social structures with Socialize and Bureaucracy Charms in a way that Lunars just shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps if on the nature to manipulate the &quot;alpha&quot; or pack leader? I know they aren't the animal exalted, but one of their social things could be inspired by pack animal mentality. Nature has a societal hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T23:10:19-07:00","id":110619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110585#post110585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps if on the nature to manipulate the &quot;alpha&quot; or pack leader? I know they aren't the animal exalted, but one of their social things could be inspired by pack animal mentality. Nature has a societal hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not a Lunar will be a pack kind of player depends largely on spirit shape, and in many cases, this will result in not being one. Garou and some Fera might have had pack tactics, but this is one area where I don't see the inspiration from W:TA following over. They're more That Old Thing In the Wilderness than an entire sort of being made to be soldiers. That's the Dragon-Blooded's bag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T05:16:24-07:00","id":110717,"title":"","content":"The thing about alphas and betas and packs and pecking orders is that they are not really animal behaviors, they are human behaviors we've inexpertly applied to describe what we see in other animals. Mining them for ideas of how to manipulate humans is putting in an extra step. We already have hierarchical social structures, group-thought, and nigh-instinctive reactions waiting to be exploited. Sure we also have intelligence and reason to overcome those behaviors, but Lunars seem like an ideal exalt type to bypass that and get to the pirmal human underneath. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:20:06-07:00","id":110840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=108253#post108253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always kind of wanted a Lunar charm that caused specific people of your choice to realize that you were a shapeshifting monster in disguise, so you could gaslight them. Might be too specific, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>sounds</i> awesome, though. Replace a local official, frame someone for murder, and as he's being dragged off to prison, he looks you in the eyes and sees they are slitted, like a snake's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:26:54-07:00","id":110846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110717#post110717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about alphas and betas and packs and pecking orders is that they are not really animal behaviors, they are human behaviors we've inexpertly applied to describe what we see in other animals. Mining them for ideas of how to manipulate humans is putting in an extra step. We already have hierarchical social structures, group-thought, and nigh-instinctive reactions waiting to be exploited. Sure we also have intelligence and reason to overcome those behaviors, but Lunars seem like an ideal exalt type to bypass that and get to the pirmal human underneath.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Presuming that we're talking about wolves...<br /> <br /> It depends on usage. If you're talking about alpha as leaders, that's the hierarchy that develops in captivity. If you're talking about alphas as the parents, that's how they work in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Also, NB, on a list of things that can get you out of overcoming behavior, intelligence isn't among them, and reason among humans isn't something to be counted on - not just as infallible, but as present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:27:51-07:00","id":110849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110840#post110840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It <i>sounds</i> awesome, though. Replace a local official, frame someone for murder, and as he's being dragged off to prison, he looks you in the eyes and sees they are slitted, like a snake's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every snake has eyes slitted vertically. Cobras, for example. It's the same way with cats - housecats have the kind of pupils you're thinking of, but most big cats don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:51:23-07:00","id":110866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110846#post110846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presuming that we're talking about wolves...<br /> It depends on usage. If you're talking about alpha as leaders, that's the hierarchy that develops in captivity. If you're talking about alphas as the parents, that's how they work in the wilderness.<br /> Also, NB, on a list of things that can get you out of overcoming behavior, intelligence isn't among them, and reason among humans isn't something to be counted on - not just as infallible, but as present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually going to use that exact wolf example as a, well, example. Also pecking orders, herd mentality, etc are considerably more complex than we give them credit for. Too often when we think of as animal behavior is an oversimplification, so why use the oversimplification when we can use what humans are like when they are scared, dominated, awed, or inspired?<br /> <br /> Also intelligence is very capable of overcoming instinctive behavior, there are plenty of examples. The fact that it isn't always effective doesn't mean it isn't ever effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:57:14-07:00","id":110873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110866#post110866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was actually going to use that exact wolf example as a, well, example. Also pecking orders, herd mentality, etc are considerably more complex than we give them credit for. Too often when we think of as animal behavior is an oversimplification, so why use the oversimplification when we can use what humans are like when they are scared, dominated, awed, or inspired?<br /> <br /> Also intelligence is very capable of overcoming instinctive behavior, there are plenty of examples. The fact that it isn't always effective doesn't mean it isn't ever effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a damned good reason why Intelligence doesn't determine Will in GURPS 4th edition. Being smart doesn't protect you from your own bad habits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T10:16:37-07:00","id":110888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110873#post110873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a damned good reason why Intelligence doesn't determine Will in GURPS 4th edition. Being smart doesn't protect you from your own bad habits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No indeed, Intelligence and Willpower are different things. And if your goal is reducing the issue down to &quot;It takes willpower to overcome base instinct regardless of the reason&quot; I guess I technically can't disagree, but that is ignoring the many and varied reasons people express that willpower. Of which one is intelligence and reason.<br /> <br /> But this is getting sidetracked. My point is that Lunars stripping away resistance to get at the primal human underneath makes is a better fit for many of their social charms than making humans act like actual animals.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T10:23:47-07:00","id":110891,"title":"","content":"I wonder, since Lunar in Third Edition will draw inspiration from &quot;Mythical Monster&quot;, would they finally have eye-beam, I mean Medusa and Basilisk is a thing you know, and Second Edition does have a non-offensive &quot;Miruku Beam&quot; in the form of Eye-as-Moonbeam Method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T11:52:18-07:00","id":110957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110891#post110891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, since Lunar in Third Edition will draw inspiration from &quot;Mythical Monster&quot;, would they finally have eye-beam, I mean Medusa and Basilisk is a thing you know, and Second Edition does have a non-offensive &quot;Miruku Beam&quot; in the form of Eye-as-Moonbeam Method.</div> </div> </div> </div>A non-offensive Mikuru Beam is no Mikuru Beam at all. EaMM tended to draw more parallels from Smaug* and the Nekobus.<br /> <br /> Rankin and Bass Smaug from the old cartoon of the Hobbit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T13:19:28-07:00","id":111024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110849#post110849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not every snake has eyes slitted vertically. Cobras, for example. It's the same way with cats - housecats have the kind of pupils you're thinking of, but most big cats don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, &quot;like a python's,&quot; then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T15:33:23-07:00","id":111072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=110585#post110585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps if on the nature to manipulate the &quot;alpha&quot; or pack leader? I know they aren't the animal exalted, but one of their social things could be inspired by pack animal mentality. Nature has a societal hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So?<br /> <br /> Even without trickle-down effects, Lunars <i>can </i>still influence an entire group by influencing the leader of the group. They just can't unilaterally sway an entire group by interacting with only one individual. If a Lunar wants to impact all members of a group equally, he needs to deal with them personally, either through a single speech they all hear at once, or through a number of one-on-one interactions.<br /> <br /> That's what it means to have Charms built on social Attributes rather than the Socialize or Bureaucracy Abilities, as well as lacking &quot;perfection beyond human excellence&quot; as a theme. Holden said that Lunar Charms are meant to come off as &quot;rougher and more unpolished&quot; next to Ability-based Charms, which I imagine means lacking some of the perks of efficiency baked into Ability-based powers.<br /> <br /> The advantage is that the Lunar who learns the Charm for influencing one guy has a Charm that works equally well on any one guy, regardless of his social status or whether he has a Major or Defining positive Intimacy for the Lunar. Whereas the Solar with Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe really isn't getting the bang for his buck using that Charm on someone who isn't a leader, and would need to learn a separate Charm if he wanted to social-fu individuals who don't give a crap about him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:36:45-07:00","id":111210,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen the Lunar charmset, sadly - is there one that gives everyone around you a lust intimacy, a la pheremones?<br /> <br /> Cuz there totally should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T21:27:18-07:00","id":111239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=111210#post111210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen the Lunar charmset, sadly - is there one that gives everyone around you a lust intimacy, a la pheremones?<br /> <br /> Cuz there totally should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrifying Lust Infliction, in one of the social attributes (Charisma probably. It's been too long and I don't have the book on me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T21:41:39-07:00","id":111258,"title":"","content":"Aye, that'd be the one. That said, it's not so much via pheromones as it is just kinda making people get a hunger/lust for something (or in general) as part of a Social roll. There's no real specification or hint as to the means by which Lunars achieve this. This is either a positive or a negative depending on who you ask.<br /> <br /> Though you could probably stunt it as pheromones and still <a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0121.html\" target=\"_blank\">pull a Marena</a> just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T23:39:51-07:00","id":111308,"title":"","content":"It's a strong possibility that we'll see a Lunar pheromones Charm, because people discussed the idea with John Morke and he said it was cool.<br /> <br /> Pheromones are a very physical, primal sort of thing, and there's an Alchemical Charm called Pheromone Regulation Systems which would serve as a decent model for it. The Alchemical Charm also involves manipulating one's scent, either to become scentless (and thus harder for hounds to track) or to potentially disguise one's scent as someone or something else's, or to exude a scent that outright repels animals and strongly discomforts mortals.<br /> <br /> Given the different relationships Lunars and Alchemicals have with Charms, though, things would necessarily need to be different. And that's before answering the question of which social Attribute it really belongs to, in Third Edition's tweaked system. (Though maybe the minimums will be low enough that it won't matter?)<br /> <br /> Anyway, in Second Edition, PRS could be used all by itself to make Unnatural Mental Influence social attacks on others for the rest of the scene, but for some reason the cloud of pheromones had no other effect on anyone caught in the radius. I'd change that.<br /> <br /> I would have PRS -- Lunar and Alchemical alike -- simply involve producing a cloud of emotionally-manipulative pheromones, which affects everyone in the radius, and does absolutely nothing else on its own. If the Lunar wants to take direct magical social actions, that's what his other social Charms are for; the cloud mostly just helps him get the result he wants rather than delivering it to him in one package.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, other people can take unwitting (or witting) advantage of the emotionally-charged condition he created. That neatly turns this Charm into a hammer that the Lunar doesn't always want to use, because it can easily cause a situation to escalate faster than he planned. Again, where the Lunar wants to retain tighter control, he's better off not using this Charm and instead using more direct ones. This is good, as it keeps the pheromone Charm from being a &quot;must buy&quot; social purchase, like Irresistible Silver Spirit was (or presumably would have been, had it been as easy to use as its physical cousin, Relentless Lunar Fury).<br /> <br /> Keeping this Charm from being the cornerstone of Lunar social influence also prevents Lunar social strategy from losing its knees against someone immune or resistant to the effect, such as someone with a sense magically sharp enough to notice and reject the influence. Or someone who simply has no sense of smell at all, but then you get into the question of whether the Lunar can produce spiritual pheromones that affect such targets regardless, just as there's a Charm for spiritually smelling scents which no longer physically exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:43:28-07:00","id":111773,"title":"","content":"Vance is going to make sure some variant of First Edition's Snake Head Defense is going to make it into Third Edition.<br /> <br /> It seems very likely that Thousandfold Wasp Dance (spit up a cloud of attacking bees) and Mandate of the Hungry Mouse (turn your anima into a plague of beasts) will return.<br /> <br /> Then, perhaps Lunars might have the power to transform their discarded weapons and projectiles into creatures which rush back into their grasp? Arrows which miss their mark or boomerangs that hit it wing their way back as birds, and disarmed swords and spears become snakes that zip across the ground to return?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:49:20-07:00","id":111783,"title":"","content":"I always kinda wanted a Lunar charm where you swallow a Hearthstone, and commit one or two motes, and as long as you maintain the commitment it's like having the stone socketed in an attuned artifact, but if you relinquish the commitment the stone dissolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T22:40:35-07:00","id":111921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=111783#post111783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always kinda wanted a Lunar charm where you swallow a Hearthstone, and commit one or two motes, and as long as you maintain the commitment it's like having the stone socketed in an attuned artifact, but if you relinquish the commitment the stone dissolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as you can bring the stone back out that's interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T00:54:50-07:00","id":111949,"title":"","content":"I'd like a Charm that lets the Lunar turn her Hair/Feather/Scales into lethal weapons, like the Stymphalian Birds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T02:11:53-07:00","id":111959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=111921#post111921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So long as you can bring the stone back out that's interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Alright, alright! I'll lend you my Hearthstone. Just... gimme a couple of minutes. And some toilet paper.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T05:56:29-07:00","id":112018,"title":"","content":"It's frustrating to lack even the most basic rules for Third Edition.<br /> <br /> I want to write Charms that let the Lunar manipulate the momentum system based on their forms. If they're currently bigger than the opponent, a Charm that enhances the use of size, strength and reach for overwhelming smaller opponents. If they're currently smaller than the opponent, a Charm that enhances the use of smaller profile, evasion, agility and stealth.<br /> <br /> Because NO ONE can so easily their size relative to the opponent as the Lunar Exalted can.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, not knowing whether Knacks will return, I wonder if Towering Beast Shape will be a Charm that serves as the prerequisite for &quot;fight smaller opponents&quot;, or if &quot;fight smaller opponents&quot; might actually be the prerequisite for Towering Beast Shape.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Become The Swarm&quot; Charm might be similarly related to Charms for commanding and directing Battle Groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-13-2014, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T06:56:12-07:00","id":112030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/105041-what-should-lunars-be-able-to-do-what-should-they-not-be-able-to-do?p=111959#post111959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Alright, alright! I'll lend you my Hearthstone. Just... gimme a couple of minutes. And some toilet paper.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more reaching down their own throat and pulling it out. It's a weird detail that's unnervingly and strange like a Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T07:59:20-07:00","id":112050,"title":"","content":"Luna is a night goddess, yes ? Does that mean Lunar can fling night shrouds at people to blind them, that does suit No Moon well. How about looking at the Full Moon's anima light will give people derangements ? (I don't think anybody can got blind looking at the moon)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T16:09:59-07:00","id":112298,"title":"","content":"I have this idea for Attention-Demanding Presence.<br /> <br /> Basically, it works like the Solar Charm, Respect-Commanding Attitude, but in reverse. Rather than preventing anyone from doing anything but paying attention to a Performance action once it's begun, Attention-Demanding Presence would instead draw everyone's attention to the Lunar without the Worldwalker having to do or say anything, and their attention remains riveted on her until she actually does something.<br /> <br /> The concept is that a Lunar walks calmly into a riot and ends the chaos with her mere presence. Everyone affected falls silent and turns to look at her, sensing that someone important is about to do or say something important, and knowing exactly where to look. Even those affected individuals who don't have line of sight on her move into a position where they can see and hear her. Once she's satisfied with the size of her audience, she ends the effect by acting out, at which point she must hold their attention through her words or deeds alone.<br /> <br /> Naturally, this allows a Lunar to set the stage for a Solar who himself will use Respect-Commanding Attitude to maintain that respectful silence, but the Lunar can use it for many purposes of her own as well.<br /> <br /> It would also serve as the prerequisite to a much-more-balanced version of Cobra Hypnotic Technique, which basically <i>is </i>the Lunar version of Respect-Commanding Attitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thing is, a Lunar could also simply use Roaring Lion's Voice or whatever to shout over the noise and command everyone to pay attention to her (with some other Charm or another), which of course also reveals where they should be looking. Both the power to shout that loud and the power to strongly compel actions would be more versatile individually and together than this idea for Attention-Demanding Presence, so I'm unsure about the utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-13-2014, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}